00:34:40.010 --> 00:34:42.170
Come to pay a call on Williams. He's right across the courtyard.

00:34:42.430 --> 00:34:43.010
Better hurry up.

00:34:43.030 --> 00:34:46.070
Nice bunch of roses you sent to Earl. What do you want done with them tomorrow morning?

00:34:46.590 --> 00:34:48.010
A lot of wise guys, ain't you?

00:34:48.150 --> 00:34:50.050
You're breaking up the game, Molly. What do you want?

00:34:50.230 --> 00:34:55.050
I came to tell you what I think of you, all of you.

00:34:55.090 --> 00:34:55.770
Keep your shirt on.

00:34:56.520 --> 00:34:59.360
If you was worth breaking my nails on, I'd tear your face wide open.

00:34:59.380 --> 00:34:59.980
What do you swore about?

00:35:00.000 --> 00:35:01.720
Oh, sweetheart, wasn't that a swell story we gave you?

00:35:01.840 --> 00:35:02.540
Yeah, what do you want?

00:35:03.660 --> 00:35:05.620
Crumbs have been making a fool out of me long enough.

00:35:06.300 --> 00:35:07.940
I never said I loved Earl Williams

00:35:07.940 --> 00:35:09.540
and was willing to marry him on the gallows.

00:35:09.940 --> 00:35:12.480
You made that up about my being a soul mate

00:35:12.480 --> 00:35:13.680
and having a love nest with him.

00:35:14.320 --> 00:35:15.780
Yeah, you've been sticking around that cuckoo

00:35:15.780 --> 00:35:17.160
ever since they threw him in the death house.

00:35:17.340 --> 00:35:17.940
That's a lie.

00:35:19.780 --> 00:35:22.280
I met Mr. Williams just once in my life.

00:35:22.340 --> 00:35:22.960
How many? Two.

00:35:23.140 --> 00:35:24.640
When he was wandering around in the rain

00:35:24.640 --> 00:35:26.640
without his hat and coat on like a sick dog

00:35:26.640 --> 00:35:27.880
the day before the shooting.

00:35:27.880 --> 00:35:28.440
Give me one.

00:35:28.980 --> 00:35:29.960
I went up to him like...

00:35:30.000 --> 00:35:34.100
any human being would. And I asked him what was the matter. And he told me about being

00:35:34.100 --> 00:35:40.060
fired after being on the same job for 14 years. And I brought him up to my room because it

00:35:40.060 --> 00:35:46.650
was warm there. I'll put it on a phonograph. Oh, listen to me, please. Tell you, he just sat

00:35:46.650 --> 00:35:52.530
there talking to me all night. He never once laid a hand on me. And in the morning, he

00:35:52.530 --> 00:35:59.650
went away. I never saw him again until that day of the trial. What a witness. Are you

00:35:59.650 --> 00:35:59.970
There's a kid.

00:36:05.150 --> 00:36:06.470
Why don't you go see your boyfriend?

00:36:06.770 --> 00:36:07.810
Yeah, he's got a nice room.

00:36:07.930 --> 00:36:10.090
He won't have it long. He'll have to call for 7 a.m.

00:36:11.000 --> 00:36:13.820
I wonder a bowl of lightning don't come down and strike you all dead.

00:36:25.060 --> 00:36:25.560
What's that?

00:36:25.940 --> 00:36:27.780
They're fixing up a pain in the neck for your boyfriend.

00:36:34.860 --> 00:36:40.410
Never met nobody, no harm, sitting there this minute with the angel of death beside of a new pregnant joke.

00:36:40.410 --> 00:36:44.160
All right, now, kids, you're gonna get out of here. Now, come on. Come on, Molly, let's get out of here.

00:36:44.280 --> 00:36:46.380
Well, they ain't human. I know. They're newspaper men.

00:36:46.460 --> 00:36:51.780
All they've been doing is lying. They've been doing is writing. Why won't they listen to me?

00:37:13.790 --> 00:37:16.540
Gilder Johnson? She'll be back in a minute.

00:37:21.640 --> 00:37:22.400
Find any more cards?

00:37:22.480 --> 00:37:22.780
I had nothing.

00:37:23.310 --> 00:37:24.830
That's the use. I can't win anyway.

00:37:42.060 --> 00:37:43.160
Gentlemen of the press.

00:37:46.020 --> 00:37:48.050
Emily, going for it.

00:37:50.380 --> 00:37:50.660
Hello.

00:37:52.040 --> 00:37:52.740
Oh, hello, Bruce.

00:37:54.640 --> 00:37:54.860
What?

00:37:56.010 --> 00:37:57.730
Where are you?

00:37:57.730 --> 00:37:58.130
You're where?

00:38:00.000 --> 00:38:02.560
Never mind, never mind. I'll be right down.

00:38:08.960 --> 00:38:09.760
Sheriff, how are you doing?

00:38:09.820 --> 00:38:13.920
My chin! My back! What's going on around here?

00:38:14.040 --> 00:38:14.820
Bruce was in trouble.

00:38:15.120 --> 00:38:16.600
Lion's flushes to defend Cobb.

00:38:16.740 --> 00:38:19.120
Man forgets hanky, mama goes to wipe nose.

00:38:19.280 --> 00:38:20.920
I still give that marriage six months.

00:38:21.260 --> 00:38:23.280
I don't know what you fellas are talking about.

00:38:23.480 --> 00:38:24.200
What do you want, Pete?

00:38:26.190 --> 00:38:28.090
I've got the tickets for the hanging here, boys.

00:38:28.490 --> 00:38:28.730
Pete! Pete!

00:38:28.750 --> 00:38:29.190
What?

00:38:30.440 --> 00:38:33.520
Why can't you hang this guy at five o'clock instead of seven?

00:38:33.640 --> 00:38:35.500
Sure, it won't hurt you, and we can make the city edition.

00:38:35.780 --> 00:38:37.580
Oh, well, now, that's kind of raw, Roy.

00:38:37.760 --> 00:38:40.560
After all, I can't hang a man in his sleep just to please the newspaper.

00:38:40.700 --> 00:38:43.980
No, but you can reprieve him twice over the hangings three days before election, can't you?

00:38:44.040 --> 00:38:46.180
Well, you can run on a law and order ticket. You can do that, all right.

00:38:46.320 --> 00:38:49.120
Honest, boys, I had absolutely nothing to do with those reprieves.

00:38:49.160 --> 00:38:51.040
Yeah, how do we know there won't be another reprieve tonight?

00:38:51.200 --> 00:38:53.160
What if this Egelhubler finds Williams insane?

00:38:53.420 --> 00:38:55.460
Well, he won't find him insane because he isn't.

00:38:55.560 --> 00:38:57.000
He's just as sane as I am.

00:38:57.120 --> 00:38:57.400
Sane.

00:38:57.640 --> 00:38:59.560
Oh, now, be serious.

00:38:59.560 --> 00:38:59.960
Just boy that.

00:39:00.000 --> 00:39:02.880
After all, this is a hanging, and it's going to go according to schedule.

00:39:03.420 --> 00:39:05.500
Seven o'clock in the morning and not a minute earlier.

00:39:05.940 --> 00:39:08.120
After all, there's such a thing as being a mania.

00:39:08.180 --> 00:39:09.760
All right, Pinky, what do you want a favor?

00:39:10.150 --> 00:39:11.850
And please don't call me Pinky.

00:39:11.930 --> 00:39:12.210
Why not?

00:39:12.570 --> 00:39:15.350
Because I got a name, see, and it's Peter B. Hartwell.

00:39:15.450 --> 00:39:16.110
What's a B for?

00:39:16.250 --> 00:39:16.450
Bull.

00:39:17.520 --> 00:39:18.380
But I'm innocent.

00:39:18.580 --> 00:39:19.400
I didn't do anything.

00:39:19.560 --> 00:39:21.380
I never stole a watch in my life.

00:39:21.400 --> 00:39:22.020
No, you didn't, Bruce.

00:39:22.140 --> 00:39:22.620
I know you didn't.

00:39:22.700 --> 00:39:23.620
All right, Mike, come on, let him out.

00:39:23.700 --> 00:39:24.340
I can't, Hildy.

00:39:24.420 --> 00:39:26.700
He's accused of stealing a watch, and they found the watch on him.

00:39:26.740 --> 00:39:27.700
But I never stole...

00:39:27.700 --> 00:39:27.920
Please, Bruce.

