Hey, Mac, any dope on how he escaped?

00:46:46.320 --> 00:46:47.860
Maybe the sheriff let him out so Williams could vote for him.

00:46:47.960 --> 00:46:49.860
Oh, a man answering the description of Earl Williams

00:46:49.860 --> 00:46:51.180
was seen boarding a southbound...

00:46:51.180 --> 00:46:52.330
Call you back.

00:46:53.520 --> 00:46:54.140
What you doing?

00:46:54.300 --> 00:46:54.820
I thought so, too.

00:46:56.430 --> 00:46:57.190
Get me Walter Burns, quick.

00:47:01.050 --> 00:47:05.920
Walter, Walter, listen, the whole story on how William's got that gun in the escape and I got it exclusive.

00:47:06.580 --> 00:47:08.280
Yeah, yeah, that's right, and it's a pip.

00:47:08.860 --> 00:47:11.270
It cost me 450 bucks to tear it out of Cooley.

00:47:11.570 --> 00:47:12.670
Never mind, now, what's the story?

00:47:12.950 --> 00:47:17.290
Well, just a minute, and I'll give you the story, but I'm telling you first I had to give him all the money I had on me, and it wasn't exactly mine.

00:47:17.820 --> 00:47:19.260
Well, it's Bruce's money, and I want it back.

00:47:20.700 --> 00:47:23.960
Bruce's money? Sure, sure, sure, you'll get it. Now, what's the story?

00:47:24.580 --> 00:47:27.020
I'll send the money right down to you. I swear it on my mother's grave.

00:47:27.630 --> 00:47:29.980
All right, here's the... Wait a minute, your mother's alive.

00:47:30.220 --> 00:47:32.740
My grandmother's grave. Don't be technical, Hildy. What's the story?

00:47:33.110 --> 00:47:34.330
Well, you get that money down here.

00:47:35.260 --> 00:47:36.640
All right, all right, here's your story.

00:47:37.040 --> 00:47:38.240
The jailbreak of your dreams.

00:47:38.460 --> 00:47:41.360
It seems this expert, Dr. Egelhofer, the profound thinker from New York,

00:47:41.460 --> 00:47:43.760
was giving Williams a final sanity test in the sheriff's office.

00:47:44.100 --> 00:47:46.970
You know, sticking a lot of pins in him so that he could get his reflexes.

00:47:47.190 --> 00:47:50.090
Well, he decided to reenact the crime exactly as it had taken place

00:47:50.090 --> 00:47:52.310
in order to study Williams' powers of coordination.

00:47:52.770 --> 00:47:54.070
Well, I'm coming to it.

00:47:54.650 --> 00:47:56.450
Of course, he had to have a gun to reenact the crime with.

00:47:56.550 --> 00:47:57.770
And who do you suppose supplied it?

00:47:58.110 --> 00:47:59.330
Peter B. Hartwell.

00:47:59.490 --> 00:47:59.970
B for brain...

00:48:00.030 --> 00:48:02.750
No kidding.

00:48:04.740 --> 00:48:06.580
I'm not kidding. I'm not good enough to make this one up.

00:48:07.180 --> 00:48:09.460
Well, the sheriff gave his gun to the professor, and the professor gave it to Earl,

00:48:09.540 --> 00:48:11.380
and Earl shot the professor right in the classified ads.

00:48:11.980 --> 00:48:14.180
No ads. Ain't it perfect?

00:48:15.380 --> 00:48:17.940
If the sheriff hadn't rolled a red carpet and loaned Williams an umbrella,

00:48:18.120 --> 00:48:20.460
it couldn't have been more ideal. Who? Oh, no, no.

00:48:20.660 --> 00:48:21.680
Eggelhoffer wasn't badly hurt.

00:48:21.980 --> 00:48:24.440
They took him to the county hospital where they're awfully afraid he'll recover.

00:48:24.740 --> 00:48:26.310
Oh, that's great work, Hildy. Huh?

00:48:26.790 --> 00:48:29.310
Oh, stop worrying about the money. I'll see you get it in 15 minutes.

00:48:29.510 --> 00:48:29.970
Well, I'd better get...

00:48:30.780 --> 00:48:33.320
Bruce is downstairs waiting in a taxi cab for me, and we're in a hurry.

00:48:33.500 --> 00:48:35.940
Hold on a minute. Hey, Benji, come here.

00:48:36.480 --> 00:48:38.780
There's a guy waiting in a taxi in front of the Criminal Courts building.

00:48:38.920 --> 00:48:39.660
His name is Bruce Baldwin.

00:48:39.900 --> 00:48:40.620
What does he look like?

00:48:40.800 --> 00:48:43.520
He looks like that fellow in the movies, you know, Ralph Bellamy.

00:48:43.680 --> 00:48:44.080
Oh, him?

00:48:44.240 --> 00:48:44.680
Can you handle it?

00:48:45.160 --> 00:48:46.520
I've never fought on you yet, have I?

00:48:47.250 --> 00:48:48.750
Come on, get going. You've only got about two minutes.

00:48:49.010 --> 00:48:49.170
Hurry.

00:48:50.320 --> 00:48:51.320
Yes, dear, I'm sorry to keep you waiting.

00:48:51.520 --> 00:48:53.280
How much was it again? $450?

00:48:53.900 --> 00:48:54.560
Just a second.

00:48:55.620 --> 00:48:58.910
Louie, I need $450 worth of counterfeit money.

00:48:59.170 --> 00:48:59.910
Can't carry that much.

00:49:00.030 --> 00:49:02.570
No, just the 450 counterfeit. Where can I get it?

00:49:02.650 --> 00:49:03.470
Oh, I got that on me.

00:49:03.710 --> 00:49:05.250
Oh, kind of coincidence. Well, take it over to Hildy.

00:49:05.810 --> 00:49:06.670
Hello. It's coming right over.

00:49:06.850 --> 00:49:07.730
Yeah, I'm sending it over with Louie.

00:49:07.970 --> 00:49:10.210
Well, thanks for your story, dear, and good luck on your honeymoon.

00:49:10.590 --> 00:49:12.670
No, no, never mind the thanks. Just see how that money gets here.

00:49:17.120 --> 00:49:17.880
Hildy, you still here?

00:49:18.120 --> 00:49:19.420
No, I'm in Niagara Falls.

00:49:19.560 --> 00:49:20.220
McHugh speaking.

00:49:21.040 --> 00:49:23.650
Emo, I got a good feature for you on the manhunt. Ready?

00:49:24.270 --> 00:49:26.390
Mrs. Phoebe DeWolf, 61 1⁄2 South State Street,

00:49:26.550 --> 00:49:28.250
Colored, gave birth to a Piccaninian patrol wagon,

00:49:28.370 --> 00:49:29.890
with Sheriff Hartwell's Special Rifle Squad...

00:49:31.550 --> 00:49:34.160
Phoebe was walking along the street, went, that's right, yeah.

00:49:34.990 --> 00:49:37.110
So they coaxed her in the patrol wagon and started a race with the store.

00:49:37.490 --> 00:49:40.330
When the Piccanilly was born, the rifle squad examined him carefully...

00:49:40.330 --> 00:49:42.800
...to see if it was Earl Williams. Well, then they knew he was hiding somewhere.

00:49:44.380 --> 00:49:47.920
They named the kid Peter Hartwell DeWolf...

00:49:47.920 --> 00:49:48.300
That's room.

00:49:49.360 --> 00:49:51.800
Bruce, I thought you were downstairs in the...

00:49:51.800 --> 00:49:55.210
What? Arrested again? What for this time?

00:49:56.090 --> 00:49:58.740
Well, they called it mashing.

00:50:00.410 --> 00:50:05.200
No, I didn't, Hildy. I was sitting right in the taxi where you left me,

00:50:05.280 --> 00:50:09.110
and the young lady seemed to have a dizzy spell, and I just...

00:50:09.870 --> 00:50:14.360
Huh? Well, she's kind of, uh...

00:50:15.030 --> 00:50:19.940
Huh? Yeah, she's a blonde. Yes, very blonde.

00:50:20.360 --> 00:50:21.680
Never mind. I know how it happened. Just a minute.

00:50:21.880 --> 00:50:24.710
Give me Walter Burns. Hildy Johnson.

00:50:26.260 --> 00:50:28.620
Bruce, where are you? 27th Precinct. Hold on to me, will you?

00:50:29.530 --> 00:50:29.890
What?

00:50:31.470 --> 00:50:33.800
Well, he was there a minute ago, but I would...

00:50:34.400 --> 00:50:36.020
I'm sorry, can't locate him.

00:50:37.180 --> 00:50:38.700
Double-crossing. Hello, no, not you.

00:50:39.020 --> 00:50:40.800
Bruce, I can't get there right away.

00:50:41.020 --> 00:50:41.920
About 20 minutes.

00:50:42.540 --> 00:50:44.100
Well, you see, I have to wait here for the...

00:50:44.600 --> 00:50:45.560
I'll tell you when I see you.

00:50:46.080 --> 00:50:48.210
I can't worry if my two hands again on that wall of red...

00:50:48.210 --> 00:50:50.090
Hold in a minute, Emo. Anything I can do to help you?

00:50:50.150 --> 00:50:50.970
How much money have you got on your mind?

00:50:50.970 --> 00:50:52.950
Sorry. 64 cents. Welcome to it.

00:50:53.360 --> 00:50:54.440
Thanks. You better buy an annuity.

00:50:55.270 --> 00:50:55.890
What's that, Emo?

00:50:56.430 --> 00:50:58.190
No, I can't give you an official statement.

00:50:58.670 --> 00:50:59.970
No. Wait a minute. Here's...

00:51:00.000 --> 00:51:03.180
the mayor maybe he'll give us one how about a statement mayor don't pester me now please i've

00:51:03.180 --> 00:51:07.080
got a lot on my mind his honor won't say anything ever seen sheriff hartwell it's hard to tell your

00:51:07.080 --> 00:51:10.760
honor you see there's so many cockroaches around here whoa wait a minute wait a minute how about

00:51:10.760 --> 00:51:14.440
a statement sure we go to press in 20 minutes i can't help that i have nothing to say not at this

00:51:14.440 --> 00:51:17.880
time just a moment please what do you know about the escape how to get out where do you get the gun

00:51:17.880 --> 00:51:21.260
wait a minute boys not so fast well give us a statement on the election then what effect will

00:51:21.260 --> 00:51:25.860
all this have on the voters none whatsoever how can an unavoidable misfortune like this

00:51:25.860 --> 00:51:28.200
have any influence on the upright citizens

00:51:28.200 --> 00:51:29.180
of our fair city.

00:51:30.000 --> 00:51:32.760
Mr. Mayor, please, is there a red menace or ain't there?

00:51:32.800 --> 00:51:34.460
How did Williams get out of that rubber jail yard?

00:51:34.540 --> 00:51:37.020
Do you understand the gaff? You picked out somebody to be responsible.

00:51:37.280 --> 00:51:39.600
Is there any truth in the report that you're on Stalin's payroll?

00:51:39.840 --> 00:51:42.220
Yeah, the senator claims you sleep in red underwear.

00:51:42.440 --> 00:51:44.200
Never mind the jokes. Don't forget I'm the mayor.

00:51:44.700 --> 00:51:45.440
Oh, wait a minute. Come here, Pat.

00:51:45.760 --> 00:51:47.400
Well, I want to see you. How'd he get away?

00:51:47.500 --> 00:51:48.740
How'd he get off? Where'd he get the guns?

00:51:49.480 --> 00:51:51.500
Hi, Your Honor. Any statement on the red uprising tomorrow?

00:51:52.080 --> 00:51:53.960
What red uprising? There'll be no red uprising.

00:51:54.120 --> 00:51:57.180
The governor says the situation calls for the militia. Give me a rewrite.

00:51:57.180 --> 00:51:59.980
You can quote me as saying anything the governor says that...

00:52:00.400 --> 00:52:03.140
Yes. Hello, Jake. Here's a red-hot statement from the governor.

00:52:03.770 --> 00:52:08.270
He claims the mayor and the sheriff have shown themselves to be a couple of eight-year-olds playing with fire.

00:52:08.870 --> 00:52:11.500
Yeah. You can quote him as follows.

00:52:12.200 --> 00:52:15.200
It is a lucky thing for the city that next Tuesday is Election Day,

00:52:15.300 --> 00:52:19.200
as the citizens will thus be saved the expense of impeaching the mayor and the sheriff.

00:52:19.520 --> 00:52:22.080
That's all. I'll call you back. I still have seen you, mayor.

00:52:22.820 --> 00:52:24.340
Excuse me, boys. I've got so much time.

00:52:24.460 --> 00:52:25.360
What's going, Piggy?

00:52:25.460 --> 00:52:27.020
Who engineered this guy? Was it the Reds? No.

00:52:27.140 --> 00:52:29.960
Who was it? You? Me? No. Just a minute and I'll tell you. I've got...

00:52:30.220 --> 00:52:31.620
Who, Williams? Where? Where is he?

00:52:31.680 --> 00:52:33.560
Out on Center Street, where he used to live. I just got a tip.

00:52:33.660 --> 00:52:34.280
Well, why didn't you say so?

00:52:34.580 --> 00:52:35.940
The rifle squad's just going out.

00:52:35.980 --> 00:52:37.700
Holy swat. He'll be able to catch it if you hurry.

00:52:37.840 --> 00:52:38.840
Look, please, Pete, I want to talk to you.

00:52:38.840 --> 00:52:40.340
Please, Fred, look, I've got so much to do.

00:52:40.850 --> 00:52:41.970
Now, see here, Fred.

00:52:42.290 --> 00:52:43.050
Pete, you're through.

00:52:43.390 --> 00:52:44.790
Through? You mean I'm through?

00:52:44.910 --> 00:52:46.950
I mean I'm scratching your nail off with the ticket next Tuesday,

00:52:47.090 --> 00:52:48.370
and I'm running Sherman on your plate.

00:52:49.060 --> 00:52:50.180
Reform the red with a roll.

00:52:50.200 --> 00:52:50.640
Yeah, but Fred, I...

00:52:50.640 --> 00:52:51.980
Williams isn't a red, and you know it.

00:52:52.160 --> 00:52:54.160
But there are a lot of communistic sympathizers around,

00:52:54.260 --> 00:52:56.760
and I thought that if I got a slogan like that, I could...

00:52:56.760 --> 00:52:59.080
I know it, but that's got nothing to do with this case.

00:52:59.100 --> 00:52:59.900
Do you realize that?

00:53:00.030 --> 00:53:02.910
200,000 votes that stick, and if Earl Williams don't hang, we're going to lose him?

00:53:03.010 --> 00:53:05.530
We're going to hang him? Come in. He can't get away.

00:53:05.730 --> 00:53:07.830
What do you mean, he can't get away? He did get away, didn't he?

00:53:07.990 --> 00:53:10.020
What do you want? I, uh...

00:53:10.020 --> 00:53:12.030
What do you want? Are you Sheriff Hartwell?

00:53:12.210 --> 00:53:13.350
I'm here. What is it?

00:53:13.950 --> 00:53:17.250
You're a hard man to find, Sheriff. I have a message here from the governor.

00:53:17.450 --> 00:53:19.850
Is this it? It was a reprieve for Earl Williams.

00:53:20.010 --> 00:53:21.670
For who? Earl Williams' reprieve.

00:53:21.790 --> 00:53:23.370
And you said there wasn't going to be a reprieve.

00:53:23.430 --> 00:53:26.230
I didn't get it. It frightens me to think of what I'd like to do to you.

00:53:26.450 --> 00:53:27.610
Who else were there when he gave you this?

00:53:27.690 --> 00:53:28.850
Nobody. He was out fishing.

00:53:28.970 --> 00:53:29.770
Get the governor on the phone.

00:53:30.000 --> 00:53:32.980
No, he's not there. He's out duck-shooting, but a red hat.

00:53:34.340 --> 00:53:39.360
A guy who's done nothing for the last 40 years but play pinochle, gets elected governor, and right away thinks he's a Tarzan.

00:53:39.460 --> 00:53:42.740
Read that. Insane, he says. Why, he knows very well Williams isn't insane.

00:53:42.920 --> 00:53:43.900
Well, I never met the man.

00:53:44.160 --> 00:53:45.210
Ah, pure politics.

00:53:45.350 --> 00:53:46.150
It's an attempt to ruin us.

00:53:46.330 --> 00:53:47.030
Dementia, pray God.

00:53:47.030 --> 00:53:48.930
Fred, we've got to think fast. What are we going to tell the reporters?

00:53:49.030 --> 00:53:50.610
Tell him the party's through in this state on account of you.

00:53:50.630 --> 00:53:51.210
Oh, Fred.

00:53:51.450 --> 00:53:53.810
And as an afterthought, tell him I want your resignation now.

00:53:54.310 --> 00:53:56.250
Hello? Yes? Yes, this is Hartwell.

00:53:56.670 --> 00:53:59.660
What? Where? Where? Holy mo...

00:54:00.410 --> 00:54:01.930
They've got him. They've got Williams.

00:54:02.190 --> 00:54:03.990
They've got him surrounded, the rifle squad had out at his house.

00:54:04.130 --> 00:54:06.270
Tell him to hold the phone. Hold the wire.

00:54:06.530 --> 00:54:07.550
Cover up that transfer. Cover up.

00:54:07.710 --> 00:54:10.980
Now, listen. You never arrived with this.

00:54:11.140 --> 00:54:13.200
Yes, I did. Don't you remember? I came through that door.

00:54:13.300 --> 00:54:13.980
How much money did you make?

00:54:15.540 --> 00:54:16.880
What's your salary? $40 a week.

00:54:16.880 --> 00:54:17.360
Don't cut me off.

00:54:17.380 --> 00:54:20.540
How would you like to make $350 a month? That's almost $100 a week.

00:54:20.680 --> 00:54:22.480
No, I couldn't afford that. Who, me?

00:54:22.620 --> 00:54:25.620
Who do you think? They need a fellow like you in the city sealer's office.

00:54:25.800 --> 00:54:26.940
In the what? City sealer's.

00:54:27.100 --> 00:54:29.060
You mean I should work? No, wait a minute. I'm in conference.

00:54:29.060 --> 00:54:29.980
Well, my wife wouldn't want to.

00:54:31.140 --> 00:54:33.420
Well, you see, my wife lives in the country with my family.

00:54:33.580 --> 00:54:35.840
That's all right. You can bring her in here. We'll pay all the expenses.

00:54:36.640 --> 00:54:37.940
No, I don't think so.

00:54:37.940 --> 00:54:39.220
For heaven's sakes, why not?

00:54:39.340 --> 00:54:40.960
Well, I got two kids going to school,

00:54:41.000 --> 00:54:42.560
and if they change towns, they'll lose a grade.

00:54:42.700 --> 00:54:44.360
No, they won't. They'll skip a grade.

00:54:44.520 --> 00:54:46.940
And I'll guarantee you that they'll graduate with highest...

00:54:46.940 --> 00:54:48.500
Hold your horses also very afraid.

00:54:48.840 --> 00:54:49.400
Now, what do you say?

00:54:49.940 --> 00:54:51.940
It puts me in a kind of peculiar hole.

00:54:52.240 --> 00:54:54.140
No, it doesn't. Now, remember, you never delivered this.

00:54:54.260 --> 00:54:54.620
Yes, I did.

00:54:54.640 --> 00:54:56.460
No, you didn't. You got caught in the traffic or something.

00:54:56.620 --> 00:54:57.260
No, I came around the back.

00:54:57.260 --> 00:54:58.980
Well, pretend you didn't. Now, get out of here.

00:54:58.980 --> 00:54:59.980
Don't let anybody say...

00:55:00.030 --> 00:55:02.060
Yes, but how do I know that...

00:55:02.060 --> 00:55:03.420
Come in and see me in my office tomorrow.

00:55:03.640 --> 00:55:04.100
What's your name?

00:55:04.280 --> 00:55:04.960
Pettibone, what's yours?

00:55:05.140 --> 00:55:05.420
Pettibone?

00:55:05.520 --> 00:55:06.020
Not really.

00:55:06.260 --> 00:55:06.600
No, no, no.

00:55:06.660 --> 00:55:08.540
All you've got to do is to lay low and keep your mouth shut.

00:55:08.560 --> 00:55:09.440
Well, I'm tired, anyhow.

00:55:09.620 --> 00:55:10.460
Here, go to this address.

00:55:10.640 --> 00:55:11.420
Nice, homey place.

00:55:11.900 --> 00:55:12.760
They'll take good care of you.

00:55:12.900 --> 00:55:13.840
Just tell them Fred sent you.

00:55:14.170 --> 00:55:15.290
Here, it's $50 on a copy.

00:55:15.310 --> 00:55:16.210
Will you wait all the...

00:55:16.570 --> 00:55:17.450
I'll tell you in one minute.

00:55:17.610 --> 00:55:19.130
Oh, you forgot to tell me what a city city does.

00:55:19.150 --> 00:55:19.910
I'll explain it all tomorrow.

00:55:20.010 --> 00:55:20.490
Is it hard?

00:55:20.670 --> 00:55:21.790
No, no, easy, very easy.

00:55:21.870 --> 00:55:24.110
Well, that's good, because my health isn't what my wife...

00:55:24.110 --> 00:55:24.930
Well, we'll fix that, too.

00:55:30.030 --> 00:55:32.190
Tell him to shoot to kill. What? You heard what I said.

00:55:32.330 --> 00:55:35.190
But the reprieve, Fred. I tell you. All right. Hello, Olsen.

00:55:35.610 --> 00:55:38.270
Shoot to kill. That's the orders. Pass the word alive.

00:55:38.350 --> 00:55:41.590
$500 reward. $500 to the man who does it. All right. I'll be right over.

00:55:44.600 --> 00:55:47.860
Hi, Hildy. Double-crossing hyena. What's the matter, Hildy?

00:55:47.960 --> 00:55:50.120
Don't give me that innocent stuff. What did you pull on Mr. Baldwin this time?

00:55:50.220 --> 00:55:51.900
Who, me? Yes, you and that albino of yours.

00:55:52.060 --> 00:55:54.240
Is he talking about Evangeline? None other. She ain't no albino.

00:55:54.280 --> 00:55:56.140
She'll do till one comes along. She was born right here in this country.

00:55:56.530 --> 00:55:58.570
If she tries anything else, she'll have to stay right here. I don't mind.

00:55:58.670 --> 00:55:59.870
And you too, and it won't be on a phony charge.

00:56:00.000 --> 00:56:00.990
Did you bring that money?

00:56:01.550 --> 00:56:03.330
Oh, yeah. 400 bucks.

00:56:04.500 --> 00:56:04.820
450.

00:56:05.650 --> 00:56:07.550
All right. You can't blame a guy for trying.

00:56:08.530 --> 00:56:09.410
You'd better give me a receipt.

00:56:09.530 --> 00:56:10.350
I'll give you a scarf.

00:56:10.550 --> 00:56:11.210
I've got plenty of them.

00:56:11.330 --> 00:56:13.490
Oh, and I'll take Mr. Baldwin's wallet, too.

00:56:13.670 --> 00:56:14.370
Mr. Baldwin's what?

00:56:14.470 --> 00:56:15.550
His purse. Come on, come on, Louie.

00:56:16.620 --> 00:56:19.500
All right, Hilde. I'll do it for you because I like you.

00:56:19.660 --> 00:56:22.420
But you'd better tell that financier to be more careful in these hard times.

00:56:22.580 --> 00:56:23.200
Sure, sure.

00:56:23.700 --> 00:56:25.260
Want to load them a pair of your brass knuckles, too?

00:56:25.400 --> 00:56:28.260
Don't talk that way, Hilde. Here, I'll take that. I'll take it in the station.

00:56:28.440 --> 00:56:29.400
Wait a minute, wait a minute.

00:56:30.680 --> 00:56:33.220
You'll take it to the 27th precinct and tell the cops how this all happened.

00:56:33.240 --> 00:56:35.180
I couldn't do that, Hildy. Boys would have me an albatress in an hour.

00:56:35.320 --> 00:56:35.960
That's not a bad idea.

00:56:36.080 --> 00:56:36.320
Here, catch.

00:56:37.020 --> 00:56:37.340
Louie!

00:56:46.840 --> 00:56:48.600
Hello, operator. Hildy Johnson, will you get me...

00:56:49.390 --> 00:56:50.170
Drop that phone.

00:56:51.100 --> 00:56:51.680
Never mind.

00:56:53.270 --> 00:56:54.910
You're not gonna tell anybody where I am.

00:56:59.140 --> 00:56:59.980
That gun down her...

00:57:03.390 --> 00:57:04.930
Shoot me, Earl. I'm your friend, remember?

00:57:05.680 --> 00:57:07.780
I'm going to write the story on you of production for use.

00:57:08.020 --> 00:57:10.490
Oh, yes. That's right. Production for use.

00:57:11.290 --> 00:57:12.230
You don't want to hurt your friend.

00:57:12.330 --> 00:57:14.600
Don't move. Maybe you're my friend and maybe you're not.

00:57:14.860 --> 00:57:15.780
But don't come any near.

00:57:16.260 --> 00:57:18.120
You can't trust anybody in this crazy world.

00:57:19.690 --> 00:57:22.290
Blame, Earl. If I were you, I wouldn't trust anybody either.

00:57:22.410 --> 00:57:24.010
Don't do that. Put it back. Put it back.

00:57:25.020 --> 00:57:26.980
You know, if you try any tricks, I'll shoot you.

00:57:27.260 --> 00:57:28.320
I can do it right from here.

00:57:30.780 --> 00:57:33.710
You don't want to do that. You don't want to kill anybody.

00:57:34.560 --> 00:57:36.830
No, you're right. I don't want to kill anybody.

00:57:38.100 --> 00:57:39.860
I thought. Wait a minute. Where are you going?

00:57:40.880 --> 00:57:42.940
I was just going to close the door so nobody would see you.

00:57:43.120 --> 00:57:44.960
No, you weren't. You were going to get somebody.

00:57:45.240 --> 00:57:47.710
But I don't want that. All I want is to be left alone.

00:57:47.770 --> 00:57:50.290
I won't get anybody. Yes, you will. You'll get them after me again.

00:57:50.430 --> 00:57:51.270
I won't let you do that.

00:57:52.110 --> 00:57:56.350
I'm getting so tired of all the shells.

00:57:58.020 --> 00:57:59.880
I'm awful tired. I couldn't go.

00:58:01.200 --> 00:58:03.890
I don't care. I'm not afraid to die.

00:58:04.580 --> 00:58:06.600
I was telling the fellow that when he handed me the gun.

00:58:06.860 --> 00:58:08.640
He's waking me up in the middle of the night,

00:58:08.890 --> 00:58:10.830
talking to me about things they don't understand.

00:58:10.990 --> 00:58:11.230
Shut up.

00:58:11.960 --> 00:58:14.250
I wish they'd take me back and hang me.

00:58:14.290 --> 00:58:15.570
They will if you don't keep quiet.

00:58:16.050 --> 00:58:18.030
I couldn't go through another day like this.

00:58:18.150 --> 00:58:19.150
Maybe I think I could.

00:58:20.240 --> 00:58:22.540
Give me Walter Burns, quick. Tell him I need him.

00:58:23.650 --> 00:58:27.070
Oh, but, Bruce, please.

00:58:27.520 --> 00:58:29.280
I know I said to be down 20 years, but something terrific has happened.

00:58:29.400 --> 00:58:29.620
Hold on.

00:58:30.280 --> 00:58:32.580
Hildy, come over here right away. Wait, Bruce, just a second, I'll explain everything.

00:58:32.860 --> 00:58:35.100
Walter, get this. I've got Earl Williams here. Yeah, right in the press room.

00:58:35.280 --> 00:58:36.560
Honest, on the level. Hurry, I need you. Right.

00:58:37.060 --> 00:58:38.700
Bruce, the biggest thing in the world has happened. I've captured Earl Williams.

00:58:38.820 --> 00:58:40.630
You know, the murderer. Stay down there, Earl.

00:58:40.910 --> 00:58:42.590
Wait a minute. Listen, Bruce, I'll be down.

00:58:42.750 --> 00:58:44.170
But just as soon as I hand them over the paper, I'll be right down.

00:58:44.630 --> 00:58:46.590
Bruce, I can't. Bruce, don't you realize that...

00:58:47.270 --> 00:58:53.960
Who is it? I've got to find...

00:58:55.130 --> 00:58:56.550
Is everybody? Well, they're not here. They've all gone.

00:58:56.670 --> 00:58:58.450
Oh, please tell me where they've gone. Please tell me.

00:58:58.510 --> 00:58:59.750
Molly, I don't know. And I'm awfully busy.

00:59:00.000 --> 00:59:03.120
Oh, look. They got him surrounded. They're gonna shoot him down like a dog.

00:59:03.240 --> 00:59:04.720
They're looking for you, too. If you're smart, get out of here.

00:59:04.760 --> 00:59:07.640
I don't care. You gotta tell me. I ain't afraid of them.

00:59:07.700 --> 00:59:09.960
Molly, I'll tell you where they are. They're down at Center Street. Center and Fourth.

00:59:10.280 --> 00:59:11.220
Oh, that's where he used to...

00:59:11.220 --> 00:59:12.900
Molly. Molly, don't go.

00:59:13.120 --> 00:59:14.720
Oh, come in, Molly. Drop a chair.

00:59:18.330 --> 00:59:19.810
Molly. Get in here.

00:59:20.070 --> 00:59:20.670
Down the pipe.

00:59:21.290 --> 00:59:23.560
I didn't mean to shoot him. Really, I didn't.

00:59:23.820 --> 00:59:26.550
Shh, Molly.

00:59:27.920 --> 00:59:29.970
Thanks for the roses. They were beautiful.

00:59:36.650 --> 00:59:38.130
I want to get him out of here.

00:59:38.150 --> 00:59:39.070
Sit down, you crazy.

00:59:39.290 --> 00:59:40.900
You wouldn't get off way down that hole without being seen.

00:59:41.580 --> 00:59:43.320
I know what I do.

00:59:43.420 --> 00:59:44.180
Before those reporters come back.

00:59:44.630 --> 00:59:45.350
Let him take me.

00:59:45.490 --> 00:59:46.390
What difference does it make?

00:59:46.490 --> 00:59:47.270
No, I'll never let him.

00:59:49.080 --> 00:59:50.020
Hey, who locked the door?

00:59:52.310 --> 00:59:53.170
No, it isn't.

00:59:53.250 --> 00:59:54.010
Earl, get in this desk.

00:59:54.070 --> 00:59:54.550
Oh, what do you mean?

00:59:54.550 --> 00:59:55.310
Come on, get in.

01:00:11.670 --> 01:00:14.150
You're getting kind of exclusive, after all. We've got some phone calls to me.

01:00:14.490 --> 01:00:15.910
What's she doing up here? Run down and get some smelling salts.

01:00:16.010 --> 01:00:16.590
What's the matter?

01:00:17.240 --> 01:00:19.360
Came up here and had hysterics. Got pretty sick.

01:00:19.520 --> 01:00:20.260
How do you feel, Kit?

01:00:20.520 --> 01:00:21.520
I don't feel so good.

01:00:21.600 --> 01:00:22.140
Get you some water?

01:00:22.340 --> 01:00:22.800
I'll get it.

01:00:22.860 --> 01:00:23.520
Do anything for you?

01:00:23.640 --> 01:00:23.900
No.

01:00:24.260 --> 01:00:25.360
You don't look so sick to me.

01:00:25.440 --> 01:00:26.620
You didn't bump into Williams, did you?

01:00:26.800 --> 01:00:27.620
Ain't you funny?

01:00:27.780 --> 01:00:28.320
Where is he?

01:00:28.480 --> 01:00:29.380
I'll be alone, will you?

01:00:29.520 --> 01:00:29.820
Okay.

01:00:30.000 --> 01:00:31.560
Hey, give me the desk. No harm in asking.

01:00:32.050 --> 01:00:33.950
Hello, Jim? Yes, false alarm.

01:00:34.210 --> 01:00:37.570
They surrounded the house, all right, but they forgot to tell Williams, and he wasn't there.

01:00:37.730 --> 01:00:40.090
Halloween going on outside, the whole police force standing on its ear.

01:00:40.210 --> 01:00:41.290
Oh, hello, Hilde, I thought you were gone.

01:00:41.410 --> 01:00:43.970
I've been waiting for some money from Walden. What a chase. Give me Emo.

01:00:43.990 --> 01:00:44.590
What was wrong, Williams?

01:00:45.750 --> 01:00:46.690
Any news, boys?

01:00:46.930 --> 01:00:49.280
Yeah. I've never been so tired in my life.

01:00:49.340 --> 01:00:51.060
What? Where? Melrose Station? Huh?

01:00:51.240 --> 01:00:52.800
All right, connect me. Hello, Molly, how are you?

01:00:52.960 --> 01:00:54.500
Hold in a minute. Hey, fellas, this looks good.

01:00:54.600 --> 01:00:55.140
Yeah, call you back.

01:00:55.280 --> 01:00:58.300
An old lady just called Detective Buren, claims Williams is hiding under her piazza.

01:00:58.360 --> 01:00:59.080
Tell her to stand up.

01:00:59.080 --> 01:00:59.960
I'm gonna look that way out of-

01:01:00.160 --> 01:01:00.980
Do you want to go out on it?

01:01:01.180 --> 01:01:02.780
I have to stick around. I'll cover this in for you.

01:01:03.040 --> 01:01:04.920
I spent $1.40 on taxi cabs already.

01:01:05.040 --> 01:01:06.160
Let's not do any more going out.

01:01:06.260 --> 01:01:07.340
Never mind, Sarge. Tear it up.

01:01:07.460 --> 01:01:08.460
Say, who pulled the shades down?

01:01:08.600 --> 01:01:10.140
I did. They were throwing those lights around.

01:01:17.370 --> 01:01:20.540
I got a hunch Williams ain't anywhere they've been looking for him.

01:01:21.100 --> 01:01:22.600
Might be right here in this building somewhere.

01:01:23.040 --> 01:01:25.680
Sure, sure. Hanging around like a duck in a shooting gallery.

01:01:26.260 --> 01:01:28.600
There's that skylight he got out of, but how did he reach the ground?

01:01:28.820 --> 01:01:29.980
I'm pretending there ain't any.

01:01:30.000 --> 01:01:34.540
over this roof it's only about four feet yeah once he got to the roof you could slide down

01:01:34.540 --> 01:01:38.800
a drain pipe and come in any one of these windows on this side the story's gonna walk right in the

01:01:38.800 --> 01:01:42.460
window masterminds at work why don't you boys go home maybe williams will come and call on you

01:01:42.460 --> 01:01:46.040
wouldn't it be funny if he's in this building somewhere why not search the building everybody

01:01:46.040 --> 01:01:50.060
take a floor i'm not going to wander all over this place a great bunch of reporters you are

01:01:50.060 --> 01:01:53.920
the biggest story in two years and you're all too lazy to go out say hilly if i know you you seem

01:01:53.920 --> 01:01:57.580
pretty anxious to get rid of us you trying to scoop us or something what is it on my own time

01:01:57.580 --> 01:01:59.620
Molly's been giving her the story on how Williams got the gun.

01:02:00.060 --> 01:02:01.460
Did you smuggle that gun into Williams, Molly?

01:02:01.680 --> 01:02:02.680
No, I didn't do nothing.

01:02:02.780 --> 01:02:03.320
Come clean, Molly.

01:02:03.920 --> 01:02:04.580
Lily, let the girl alone.

01:02:04.900 --> 01:02:05.200
Will?

01:02:06.570 --> 01:02:07.750
Baldwin! Mother!

01:02:08.110 --> 01:02:10.790
Don't you mother me, playing cat and mouse with my poor boy,

01:02:10.890 --> 01:02:13.070
keeping him locked up, making us miss two trains,

01:02:13.210 --> 01:02:14.450
and you supposed to be married tomorrow.

01:02:14.790 --> 01:02:15.630
I'll be with you in five minutes.

01:02:15.650 --> 01:02:17.070
You don't have to go with me at all.

01:02:17.210 --> 01:02:18.090
Just give me Bruce's money.

01:02:18.230 --> 01:02:20.030
You can stay here forever, as far as I'm concerned.

01:02:20.210 --> 01:02:20.790
Mother, please.

01:02:20.790 --> 01:02:21.690
You and that murderer you caught.

01:02:21.810 --> 01:02:22.130
What's that?

01:02:22.750 --> 01:02:24.010
Which one of these men is it?

01:02:24.130 --> 01:02:25.690
They all look like murderers to me.

01:02:25.770 --> 01:02:27.190
Wait a minute, Hildy. What murderer did you catch?

01:02:27.910 --> 01:02:29.070
I never said any such thing.

01:02:29.070 --> 01:02:29.970
I'm quoting my

01:02:30.000 --> 01:02:31.680
My son, and he has never lied to me.

01:02:32.060 --> 01:02:34.440
That's ridiculous. This is the first place. I never said anything like that.

01:02:34.480 --> 01:02:35.160
Yes, you did.

01:02:35.280 --> 01:02:37.680
No, I didn't. I said I was trying to find the murderer.

01:02:38.100 --> 01:02:39.780
She's got it all balled up. Can't you see that?

01:02:39.940 --> 01:02:40.340
Who are you holding on?

01:02:40.940 --> 01:02:41.260
Nobody.

01:02:41.580 --> 01:02:43.600
Now, let me go, William. I don't know where he is.

01:02:43.700 --> 01:02:44.740
Stop it. Stop it.

01:02:45.340 --> 01:02:47.720
What are you asking her for? She don't know where he is.

01:02:48.120 --> 01:02:49.260
I'm the only one that knows.

01:02:49.500 --> 01:02:50.060
Where is William?

01:02:50.340 --> 01:02:51.040
Try and find out.

01:02:51.140 --> 01:02:51.840
Come on, Molly. Talk.

01:02:52.080 --> 01:02:53.810
Talk? Now you want me to talk?

01:02:53.890 --> 01:02:54.030
Sure.

01:02:54.520 --> 01:02:55.320
Oh, ain't that funny?

01:02:55.540 --> 01:02:57.640
You wouldn't listen to me before, not even for a minute.

01:02:57.900 --> 01:02:59.020
Now you want me to talk.

01:02:59.140 --> 01:02:59.880
Don't tell him anything, Molly.

01:03:01.080 --> 01:03:01.860
Stay out of there, Sylvie.

01:03:02.140 --> 01:03:03.200
Why didn't you listen to me?

01:03:03.500 --> 01:03:04.320
Come on, cut that out.

01:03:04.520 --> 01:03:05.640
You keep your hands off of me.

01:03:05.640 --> 01:03:05.820
Where is he?

01:03:06.040 --> 01:03:07.000
What do you want to know for?

01:03:07.180 --> 01:03:08.440
So you can write some more lies,

01:03:08.640 --> 01:03:09.680
so you can sell some more papers.

01:03:09.760 --> 01:03:10.340
Never mind, Dad.

01:03:10.780 --> 01:03:11.440
All right, all right.

01:03:11.500 --> 01:03:12.180
I'll tell you what I'll do.

01:03:12.260 --> 01:03:13.100
I'll give you a story.

01:03:13.240 --> 01:03:14.380
I'll give you a wonderful story.

01:03:15.160 --> 01:03:15.920
It'll be true.

01:03:16.360 --> 01:03:17.420
You'll never find him now.

01:03:18.720 --> 01:03:19.780
Get the ambulance somebody.

01:03:20.340 --> 01:03:21.200
Get the ambulance somebody.

01:03:21.380 --> 01:03:26.160
She's dead.

01:03:26.790 --> 01:03:27.530
Well, she isn't killed.

01:03:27.630 --> 01:03:27.990
She's moving.

01:03:33.070 --> 01:03:34.730
Darling, did you see that? She jumped out the window.

01:03:35.410 --> 01:03:36.210
She isn't dead.

01:03:36.590 --> 01:03:37.670
Where have you got Williams?

01:03:38.270 --> 01:03:40.680
He's in the desk. She didn't kill us.

01:03:41.510 --> 01:03:42.910
Let me out. I can't stand it.

01:03:42.970 --> 01:03:43.930
Keep quiet. You're sitting pretty.

01:03:44.620 --> 01:03:45.200
What's in there?

01:03:45.740 --> 01:03:48.060
What are you doing? This is Mrs. Baldwin, Bruce's mother.

01:03:48.640 --> 01:03:50.940
Shut up. You're doing something wrong.

01:03:51.340 --> 01:03:51.900
Take her out of here.

01:03:52.580 --> 01:03:54.860
Quiet. Louie, take the lady over to Pollock Mike's.

01:03:54.900 --> 01:03:55.800
My name's Louie Peluso.

01:03:58.400 --> 01:03:59.860
Lock her up. She doesn't talk to anyone.

01:04:01.020 --> 01:04:02.300
Tell him it's a case of DT.

01:04:02.420 --> 01:04:02.960
Don't worry, Mother.

01:04:03.440 --> 01:04:03.760
He can't run.

01:04:05.570 --> 01:04:06.050
Let go of me.

01:04:06.270 --> 01:04:07.970
Where do you think you're going?

01:04:08.110 --> 01:04:09.930
I'm going after Mother, and I'm going to get Bruce out of jail.

01:04:10.130 --> 01:04:11.950
Waldo, why did you have to do this to me?

01:04:12.130 --> 01:04:13.520
Get Bruce out of jail?

01:04:13.560 --> 01:04:14.880
How can you worry about a man who's...

01:04:15.000 --> 01:04:16.240
in a nice quiet police station.

01:04:16.340 --> 01:04:17.900
Well, this is going on hilly. This is war.

01:04:18.040 --> 01:04:18.860
You can't desert me now.

01:04:18.860 --> 01:04:20.140
Oh, get off that trapeze.

01:04:20.140 --> 01:04:21.420
You've got your story right over there on the desk.

01:04:21.560 --> 01:04:22.780
Go on, smear it all over the front page.

01:04:22.860 --> 01:04:24.180
Gerald Williams captured by the Morning Post.

01:04:24.360 --> 01:04:25.520
I covered your story for you,

01:04:25.540 --> 01:04:27.140
and I got in a fine mess doing it. Now I'm getting out.

01:04:27.260 --> 01:04:28.500
You drooling idiot. What do you mean?

01:04:28.560 --> 01:04:29.220
I just what I said.

01:04:30.028 --> 01:04:36.748
365 days in a year one can get mad how many times you got a murderer locked up in a desk once in a lifetime hilly you got the whole city by the seat of the pants

01:04:36.748 --> 01:04:40.908
i know i know you know you got the brain of a pancake this isn't just a story you're covering

01:04:40.908 --> 01:04:45.068
it's a revolution this is the greatest yarn in journalism since livingston discovered stanley

01:04:45.068 --> 01:04:48.428
the other way around oh well don't get technical at a time like this do you realize what you've done

01:04:48.428 --> 01:04:52.348
honey you've taken a city that's been graft-ridden for 40 years under the same old gang with this yarn

01:04:52.348 --> 01:04:55.388
you're kicking him out you're giving us a chance to have the same kind of government new york's having

01:04:56.524 --> 01:04:57.024
Listen, honey.

01:04:57.580 --> 01:05:00.000
If I didn't have your best interest at heart, you think I'd waste my time arguing?

01:05:00.284 --> 01:05:03.484
You've done something big, Hilda. You've stepped up into a new class.

01:05:03.564 --> 01:05:03.744
Huh?

01:05:04.476 --> 01:05:06.616
We'll make such monkeys out of those ward healers next Tuesday.

01:05:06.696 --> 01:05:08.216
Nobody will vote for them, not even their wives.

01:05:08.376 --> 01:05:08.916
Exposed me.

01:05:09.056 --> 01:05:10.476
Certainly. We'll crucify that mob.

01:05:10.556 --> 01:05:11.916
We'll keep Williams undercover until morning

01:05:11.916 --> 01:05:13.376
so the post can break the story exclusive.

01:05:13.516 --> 01:05:14.696
Then we'll let the governor in on the capture.

01:05:14.816 --> 01:05:15.676
Share the glory with it.

01:05:15.696 --> 01:05:16.356
I get it. I get it.

01:05:16.376 --> 01:05:18.216
You kicked over the whole city hall like an apricot.

01:05:18.276 --> 01:05:19.976
You've got the man heart well backed up against the war.

01:05:20.036 --> 01:05:21.796
You've put one administration out and another one in.

01:05:22.156 --> 01:05:23.736
This isn't just a newspaper story, Hilde.

01:05:23.796 --> 01:05:24.456
It's a career.

01:05:25.020 --> 01:05:28.360
And you stand there belly aching about whether you catch an 8 o'clock train or a 9 o'clock train.

01:05:28.360 --> 01:05:29.460
But, Mama, I never figured it that way.

01:05:29.460 --> 01:05:29.980
You're still a dolphin.

01:05:30.000 --> 01:05:32.000
Gee, he'd be the white-haired boy.

01:05:32.080 --> 01:05:34.480
There'll be streets after you. Hildy Johnson Street.

01:05:34.560 --> 01:05:36.800
There'll be statues in the park. The movies will be after you.

01:05:36.880 --> 01:05:38.720
By tomorrow morning, there's a Hildy Johnson cigar.

01:05:38.800 --> 01:05:40.000
You can see the billboards now.

01:05:40.080 --> 01:05:42.800
Will you stop that acting? We've got a lot to do.

01:05:42.880 --> 01:05:44.000
How are you talking?

01:05:44.080 --> 01:05:45.200
We can't leave Williams in here.

01:05:45.280 --> 01:05:47.120
We'll take you over to my private office. Which is our phone?

01:05:47.200 --> 01:05:49.200
That one on the end. How are you going to take him?

01:05:49.280 --> 01:05:51.200
If he's inside the desk, we'll carry the desk over.

01:05:51.280 --> 01:05:53.200
You can't move that desk. He's crawling with cops outside.

01:05:53.280 --> 01:05:54.640
We're lowering out the window with pulleys.

01:05:54.720 --> 01:05:56.080
Now quit stalling. Get the typewriter over here.

01:05:56.160 --> 01:05:57.200
Stop pounding on a lead.

01:05:57.280 --> 01:05:58.080
How much of this stuff do you want?

01:05:58.160 --> 01:05:59.040
All the words you got.

01:05:59.392 --> 01:05:59.832
Give me Duffy.

01:06:01.852 --> 01:06:03.052
Call him anything you like.

01:06:03.052 --> 01:06:04.852
How about the time he had his house painted by the fire department?

01:06:04.852 --> 01:06:05.852
Keep him to work.

01:06:05.852 --> 01:06:06.852
Hello, Duffy, get set.

01:06:06.852 --> 01:06:08.852
We got the biggest story in years.

01:06:08.852 --> 01:06:11.852
Earl Williams captured by the Morning Post exclusive.

01:06:12.156 --> 01:06:13.576
And I want you to tear out the whole front page.

01:06:13.916 --> 01:06:15.516
That's why they sent the whole front page out.

01:06:15.900 --> 01:06:18.320
Well, never mind the European war. We got something a whole lot bigger than that.

01:06:18.640 --> 01:06:20.420
Hilda Johnson's right in the lead. I'll give it to you as soon as she's finished.

01:06:20.764 --> 01:06:22.764
And listen, Duffy, get hold of Butch O'Connor.

01:06:22.864 --> 01:06:24.904
Time to come up here right away with half a dozen of his wrestlers.

01:06:25.184 --> 01:06:26.044
Yeah, Butch O'Connor.

01:06:26.396 --> 01:06:28.376
What? Well, I got a disc I want, Lou. Never mind.

01:06:28.476 --> 01:06:29.976
Tell me. What the juice do you want?

01:06:31.468 --> 01:06:33.748
Oh, no, never mind the Chinese earthquake, for heaven's sake.

01:06:33.768 --> 01:06:35.268
Hildy, I just want to ask you one question.

01:06:35.288 --> 01:06:36.328
Bruce, how did you get out of jail?

01:06:36.368 --> 01:06:37.248
Well, not through any help but yours.

01:06:37.248 --> 01:06:38.648
Now, listen, buddy, you can't come in here.

01:06:38.648 --> 01:06:39.188
I'm not talking to you.

01:06:39.648 --> 01:06:42.628
I had to wire Albany for $100 so I could get out on bail.

01:06:42.728 --> 01:06:44.148
Look, I don't care if there's a million dead.

01:06:44.188 --> 01:06:45.768
I don't know what they're going to think up there in Albany.

01:06:45.828 --> 01:06:47.408
They had to send the money to the police station.

01:06:47.448 --> 01:06:48.668
Oh, for Pete's sake, Hildy, come on.

01:06:48.688 --> 01:06:49.428
We're waiting for that story.

01:06:49.488 --> 01:06:50.908
Yeah, we'll explain everything to them, Bruce.

01:06:50.968 --> 01:06:52.448
Where's mother? She said she was coming up here.

01:06:52.448 --> 01:06:52.848
Oh, she left.

01:06:52.888 --> 01:06:53.728
No, I can't hear you, Duffy.

01:06:53.828 --> 01:06:54.288
Where'd she go?

01:07:00.000 --> 01:07:00.960
Never mind that. This is more important.

01:07:01.000 --> 01:07:01.940
Did you get the money from you?

01:07:02.020 --> 01:07:02.980
No, no. She left in a hurry.

01:07:03.320 --> 01:07:04.420
I'll take that money, Hilary.

01:07:04.420 --> 01:07:05.380
All right, Bruce. Right there in my purse.

01:07:05.400 --> 01:07:08.400
I decided I can handle things around here, and I'll take that certified check, too.

01:07:08.460 --> 01:07:09.440
I'll give it to you, Bruce. Here.

01:07:09.620 --> 01:07:11.240
Here's the ticket, and you'll find your money in the wallet.

01:07:11.460 --> 01:07:13.480
My wallet? This is my wallet.

01:07:14.420 --> 01:07:14.980
Say, the...

01:07:15.000 --> 01:07:16.120
There's something funny going on.

01:07:16.200 --> 01:07:16.960
Here, what are you doing?

01:07:17.200 --> 01:07:18.140
Just wanted to look at it.

01:07:21.480 --> 01:07:23.040
Hildy, I'm taking the 9 o'clock train.

01:07:23.180 --> 01:07:23.900
Sure, sure.

01:07:24.100 --> 01:07:25.220
Did you hear what I said?

01:07:25.360 --> 01:07:27.780
I said I'm taking the 9 o'clock train.

01:07:27.900 --> 01:07:29.100
Oh, Bruce, I put it in here.

01:07:31.690 --> 01:07:32.740
Let her alone, will you, buddy?

01:07:33.020 --> 01:07:34.060
Will you do me a favor, Bruce, please?

01:07:34.060 --> 01:07:35.580
I just want you to answer me one question.

01:07:35.780 --> 01:07:37.280
You don't want to come with me.

01:07:37.280 --> 01:07:37.760
I need that.

01:07:38.100 --> 01:07:38.780
Answer me, Hilly.

01:07:38.840 --> 01:07:39.640
You don't, do you?

01:07:39.700 --> 01:07:39.940
No.

01:07:40.360 --> 01:07:42.520
Take all those Miss America pictures off, face it.

01:07:42.600 --> 01:07:43.060
Hilly, tell me.

01:07:43.060 --> 01:07:44.060
Please tell me the truth.

01:07:44.340 --> 01:07:44.860
Oh, wait.

01:07:45.000 --> 01:07:46.040
You have to be healthy.

01:07:46.140 --> 01:07:47.380
Now look here, my good man.

01:07:47.480 --> 01:07:48.260
You shut up, Burns.

01:07:48.400 --> 01:07:49.380
How can I do anything to you?

01:07:49.380 --> 01:07:50.440
You're doing all this to her.

01:07:50.480 --> 01:07:50.940
I know that.

01:07:51.020 --> 01:07:53.040
She wanted to get away from you and everything you stand for,

01:07:53.080 --> 01:07:53.840
but you were too smart.

01:07:53.860 --> 01:07:55.020
You caught her and changed her mind.

01:07:55.140 --> 01:07:57.120
Take Hitler and stick him on the funny page.

01:07:57.420 --> 01:07:59.300
Now let me ask you, mister, whatever your name is.

01:07:59.420 --> 01:07:59.980
For a man like...

01:08:00.000 --> 01:08:02.360
No, I'm not. Can't you see that something's happened?

01:08:02.440 --> 01:08:03.060
Wait, I'll tell you everything.

01:08:03.140 --> 01:08:05.100
Tell him! You tell him nothing! He's a spy, you fool!

01:08:05.260 --> 01:08:05.980
I'm not a spy.

01:08:06.420 --> 01:08:08.100
Come on, Hilda, you're coming with me right now.

01:08:08.300 --> 01:08:10.820
Give me just a second, can't you? Don't you see this is the biggest thing in my life?

01:08:10.920 --> 01:08:11.280
Keep quiet, honey.

01:08:11.280 --> 01:08:14.380
I see. I'll keep. I'm like something in the icebox, aren't I?

01:08:14.460 --> 01:08:14.580
Yeah.

01:08:15.000 --> 01:08:15.620
I just don't love you.

01:08:15.620 --> 01:08:16.400
Oh, now that isn't true.

01:08:16.480 --> 01:08:18.040
Just because you won't listen to me say I don't love you,

01:08:18.060 --> 01:08:19.120
now you know that isn't the point at all.

01:08:19.240 --> 01:08:21.360
The point is that you never intended to be decent

01:08:21.360 --> 01:08:22.340
and live like a human being.

01:08:22.400 --> 01:08:22.540
What's that?

01:08:22.660 --> 01:08:23.540
All right, all right.

01:08:23.950 --> 01:08:25.810
Oh, it's so bestian jumping.

01:08:25.970 --> 01:08:27.010
I'm trying to concentrate.

01:08:27.010 --> 01:08:28.390
You're just like him and all the rest.

01:08:28.450 --> 01:08:29.750
Sure, sure, that's what I am.

01:08:30.028 --> 01:08:33.528
What? What? No, no, leave the rooster story alone. That's human interest.

01:08:33.528 --> 01:08:34.528
Did you get hold of Butcher County yet?

01:08:34.528 --> 01:08:35.528
Look, if you don't see sympathy or understanding...

01:08:35.528 --> 01:08:37.528
Okay, hold on, I understand, all right. I understand.

01:08:37.528 --> 01:08:39.528
Wait, wait, just a minute. There's only one question I want to know.

01:08:39.528 --> 01:08:40.028
What?

01:08:40.028 --> 01:08:42.028
Walter, the mayor's first wife. What was her name?

01:08:42.028 --> 01:08:43.028
You mean the one with the ward on her?

01:08:43.028 --> 01:08:43.528
Right.

01:08:43.528 --> 01:08:44.528
Fanny, what do you say, Duffy?

01:08:44.528 --> 01:08:46.528
Ah, Hilly, I don't think you ever loved me at all.

01:08:46.528 --> 01:08:49.028
Oh, never mind that. You're not working for the advertising department.

01:08:49.028 --> 01:08:52.028
Remember, if you change your mind, I'm leaving on the 9 o'clock train.

01:08:52.028 --> 01:08:53.028
Hold on, Duffy, hold on.

01:08:53.028 --> 01:08:55.028
You've got to think that I am instead of trying to change me into something else.

01:08:57.356 --> 01:08:58.216
That's the stuff.

01:08:58.316 --> 01:08:59.996
Keep it coming as fast as you can.

01:09:00.060 --> 01:09:01.860
Get back in there, you mock turtle!

01:09:03.868 --> 01:09:06.928
Well, now, Duffy, did he tell Bush and his gang to take a taxi as a matter of life and death?

01:09:07.148 --> 01:09:10.508
Good. Stay on this wire. Bush is on his way over. All we gotta do is hold out for 15 minutes.

01:09:10.568 --> 01:09:12.008
The boys will be back. They'll be coming in here to phone.

01:09:12.108 --> 01:09:12.808
I'll handle them.

01:09:15.932 --> 01:09:16.892
Now the moon's out.

01:09:21.756 --> 01:09:24.296
Tree caps is me. Don't forget. How you doing? Got enough air?

01:09:24.376 --> 01:09:25.096
Not very much.

01:09:25.176 --> 01:09:25.596
That better?

01:09:26.108 --> 01:09:26.648
They're sitting printed.

01:09:27.740 --> 01:09:29.180
How's it coming, honey? Oh, all right, I guess.

01:09:29.280 --> 01:09:30.000
Where's Bruce?

01:09:30.090 --> 01:09:32.000
Oh, he went out. Is he coming back here?

01:09:32.120 --> 01:09:34.100
Certainly. What have you got so far? Let me hear it.

01:09:35.080 --> 01:09:37.040
While hundreds of Cheryl Hartwell's paid gunmen...

01:09:37.040 --> 01:09:38.960
...storked through the city shooting innocent bystanders...

01:09:38.960 --> 01:09:40.900
...spreading their reign of terror, Earl Williams was lurking...

01:09:40.900 --> 01:09:42.720
Wait a minute. Aren't you going to mention the post?

01:09:42.900 --> 01:09:43.700
Doesn't the paper get any credit?

01:09:43.860 --> 01:09:45.300
I did that right there in the second paragraph.

01:09:45.360 --> 01:09:46.420
Who's going to read the second paragraph?

01:09:46.560 --> 01:09:48.560
Listen, honey, for ten years I'll be telling you how to write a newspaper story.

01:09:48.920 --> 01:09:49.400
Oh, I'm sorry.

01:09:49.620 --> 01:09:54.960
Why are you locking this door?

01:09:55.840 --> 01:09:56.300
Who's that?

01:09:56.480 --> 01:09:58.720
That's the door!

01:10:00.640 --> 01:10:01.480
Isn't what did you say his name was?

01:10:01.600 --> 01:10:02.740
Benziger, the Tribune.

01:10:02.880 --> 01:10:03.320
Tribune, huh?

01:10:03.940 --> 01:10:04.580
Who's in there?

01:10:06.320 --> 01:10:08.440
Haven't you any better sense than that, uh, hello.

01:10:09.020 --> 01:10:09.900
Hello, Mr. Burns.

01:10:10.120 --> 01:10:11.840
Well, quite an honor having you come over here.

01:10:11.940 --> 01:10:12.560
Hello, Benziger.

01:10:13.020 --> 01:10:13.920
Oh, you know my...

01:10:14.750 --> 01:10:16.250
Excuse me, I just want to get my...

01:10:16.250 --> 01:10:18.930
You know, you know, it's quite a coincidence seeing you tonight, isn't it, Hilde?

01:10:19.090 --> 01:10:19.530
Yes, yes.

01:10:19.730 --> 01:10:20.110
How do you mean?

01:10:20.210 --> 01:10:22.890
As a matter of fact, I was talking to R. Duffy about you just this afternoon.

01:10:23.250 --> 01:10:25.190
Really? Well, nothing detrimental, I hope.

01:10:25.230 --> 01:10:27.090
On the contrary, on the contrary.

01:10:27.210 --> 01:10:28.930
There was one swell story you had in the paper this morning.

01:10:29.090 --> 01:10:29.970
Oh, did you, uh...

01:10:30.350 --> 01:10:31.570
Do you care for the poem, Mr. Burns?

01:10:31.930 --> 01:10:33.790
The poem? The poem is great.

01:10:34.050 --> 01:10:35.230
I like the ending especially.

01:10:35.550 --> 01:10:37.270
And all is well outside his cell.

01:10:37.470 --> 01:10:39.410
But in his heart he hears the hangman calling

01:10:39.410 --> 01:10:42.610
and the gallows falling and his white-haired mother's tears.

01:10:43.910 --> 01:10:44.430
Heartbreaking?

01:10:45.090 --> 01:10:46.670
That's fine. How would you like to come and work for me?

01:10:46.950 --> 01:10:47.110
What?

01:10:47.250 --> 01:10:48.890
Yes, we can use a man like you.

01:10:48.970 --> 01:10:50.890
All we've got now are a lot of lowbrows like Johnson here.

01:10:51.050 --> 01:10:51.990
Are you serious, Mr. Burns?

01:10:52.090 --> 01:10:53.050
Serious? Wait a minute.

01:10:53.860 --> 01:10:56.480
Listen, Duffy. Duffy, I'm sending a Mr. Bensinger over to see you.

01:10:56.540 --> 01:10:57.020
A Bensinger?

01:10:57.120 --> 01:10:58.040
Oh, yeah. A Mervin, isn't it?

01:10:58.120 --> 01:10:59.640
Yeah. No, Roy. Roy V.

01:11:00.000 --> 01:11:02.300
Be Benzinger the poet.

01:11:02.460 --> 01:11:04.000
Well, of course you wouldn't know.

01:11:04.080 --> 01:11:05.540
You probably never heard of Shakespeare either.

01:11:07.780 --> 01:11:10.000
Now look, I want you to put Mr. Benzinger on the staff

01:11:10.000 --> 01:11:10.420
right away.

01:11:10.560 --> 01:11:11.560
How much getting on the Tribune, Ross?

01:11:11.740 --> 01:11:12.060
75.

01:11:12.460 --> 01:11:13.340
I'll give you 100 and a byline.

01:11:13.580 --> 01:11:14.820
Now you give him everything he wants.

01:11:15.000 --> 01:11:19.770
understand okay I want you to hustle write me a story from the point of view

01:11:19.770 --> 01:11:23.130
of the escaped man he hides cowering afraid of every sound of every light he

01:11:23.130 --> 01:11:25.690
hears footsteps as hard as going like that and all the time they're closing in

01:11:25.690 --> 01:11:29.590
now get the sense of the animal at bay sort of Jack London style exactly I'll

01:11:29.590 --> 01:11:29.890
just get my

01:11:30.000 --> 01:11:31.960
It doesn't have to rhyme, doesn't have to rhyme.

01:11:32.100 --> 01:11:34.240
Well, I'm deeply grateful, Mr. Burns.

01:11:34.480 --> 01:11:34.620
Good.

01:11:34.860 --> 01:11:35.480
It's very, uh...

01:11:35.480 --> 01:11:39.960
Oh, if you should have an opening for a war correspondent, I'd parlay a little French,

01:11:40.020 --> 01:11:40.220
you know.

01:11:40.320 --> 01:11:41.120
I'll keep you in mind.

01:11:41.460 --> 01:11:42.760
Au revoir, mon capitaine.

01:11:42.880 --> 01:11:43.120
Bonjour.

01:11:47.880 --> 01:11:48.820
White-haired mother's kid.

01:11:48.920 --> 01:11:49.800
That's a tough business.

01:11:50.120 --> 01:11:52.860
Now, listen, that fellow Benzinger's on his way over to see you right now.

01:11:53.040 --> 01:11:53.860
Handle him with kid gloves.

01:11:54.100 --> 01:11:55.140
Put him to work writing poetry.

01:11:55.420 --> 01:11:56.640
No, no, we don't want him.

01:11:56.660 --> 01:11:58.100
Just stall him along until the extra's out,

01:11:58.140 --> 01:11:59.700
then tell him his poetry smells and kick him downstairs.

01:12:00.470 --> 01:12:01.710
Crossing swine.

01:12:02.210 --> 01:12:03.770
That'll teach him a lesson. He won't quit his paper.

01:12:04.370 --> 01:12:06.660
I mean you. You double-cross anybody.

01:12:07.040 --> 01:12:11.420
Wait a minute. Bruce isn't coming back. He said he was taking the 9 o'clock train.

01:12:11.480 --> 01:12:13.460
In that case, he's gone by now. Come on, honey.

01:12:14.660 --> 01:12:15.720
Get on with the story.

01:12:15.960 --> 01:12:18.400
We ought to have our plans all finished by the time Butch gets here.

01:12:18.500 --> 01:12:21.580
You have messed up my life. What am I going to do?

01:12:22.300 --> 01:12:24.900
The window's too small. We'll have to carry the desk out of the building.

01:12:25.920 --> 01:12:28.740
What a sap I am falling for your line. They're gonna name streets after me.

01:12:29.180 --> 01:12:29.900
Yes, yes, that's what you've had.

01:12:30.000 --> 01:12:31.120
Nice rest. Now get back to work.

01:12:31.140 --> 01:12:31.960
I'm not going back to work.

01:12:32.680 --> 01:12:34.920
Who is it?

01:12:35.200 --> 01:12:36.180
It's me, boss. It's Louie.

01:12:36.670 --> 01:12:40.780
Louie? What's the matter with you?

01:12:40.800 --> 01:12:40.960
Where's this ball?

01:12:41.180 --> 01:12:41.820
What happened?

01:12:42.800 --> 01:12:43.560
Down Weston Avenue.

01:12:43.700 --> 01:12:45.020
We was going 65 miles an hour.

01:12:45.160 --> 01:12:45.600
You know what I mean?

01:12:45.720 --> 01:12:46.780
Take that mush out of your mouth.

01:12:46.820 --> 01:12:47.340
Where's the old lady?

01:12:47.580 --> 01:12:47.800
I'm telling you.

01:12:48.260 --> 01:12:49.600
We run smack into a police patrol.

01:12:49.720 --> 01:12:50.040
You know what I mean?

01:12:50.120 --> 01:12:50.880
We busted it in half.

01:12:51.060 --> 01:12:52.140
Where is she?

01:12:52.180 --> 01:12:52.400
Tell me.

01:12:52.460 --> 01:12:53.980
Can you imagine bumping into a load of cops?

01:12:54.100 --> 01:12:55.400
They come rolling out like oranges.

01:12:55.500 --> 01:12:56.260
What did you do with her?

01:12:56.460 --> 01:12:56.900
Judge me.

01:12:57.040 --> 01:12:58.360
When I come too, I was running down 34th Street.

01:12:58.380 --> 01:12:59.060
You were with her, weren't you?

01:12:59.280 --> 01:12:59.680
Was I?

01:13:00.640 --> 01:13:02.120
The driver got knocked cold.

01:13:02.720 --> 01:13:05.420
Butterfingers, I gave you an old dame to take something and you hand her over to the cops.

01:13:05.620 --> 01:13:08.370
What do you mean I handed her? The cops was on the wrong side of the street.

01:13:08.630 --> 01:13:11.330
Now everything's fine. She's probably squawking her head off on the police day.

01:13:11.350 --> 01:13:13.290
I don't think she's squawking much. You know what I mean?

01:13:13.410 --> 01:13:15.040
Don't tell me. Was she killed?

01:13:15.240 --> 01:13:16.280
Hey, was she? Did you notice?

01:13:16.680 --> 01:13:19.640
Say, listen, me with a gun on the hip and a kidnapped old lady on my hands,

01:13:19.780 --> 01:13:22.260
I'm gonna stick around asking questions from a lot of cops. You know what I mean?

01:13:22.280 --> 01:13:24.800
Dead. Dead. Oh, this is the end. Oh.

01:13:25.760 --> 01:13:27.840
It's fate, Hildy. What will be will be.

01:13:28.100 --> 01:13:29.190
What am I gonna say to Bruce?

01:13:30.600 --> 01:13:33.260
Look, honey, if he really loves you, you won't have to tell him anything.

01:13:33.560 --> 01:13:36.780
Snap out of it, would you rather have had the old dame dragging the whole police force in here?

01:13:37.000 --> 01:13:38.440
I killed her. I'm responsible.

01:13:39.570 --> 01:13:41.390
What am I gonna do? How can I ever face Bruce again?

01:13:41.630 --> 01:13:42.310
Look at me, Hildy.

01:13:43.010 --> 01:13:44.430
I am looking at you, you murderer.

01:13:44.610 --> 01:13:46.890
Now, if it was my own grandmother, I'd carry on.

01:13:47.030 --> 01:13:48.050
You know I would for the paper.

01:13:48.370 --> 01:13:49.230
Louis, where did it happen?

01:13:50.340 --> 01:13:51.360
Weston and 30 Fort.

01:13:51.680 --> 01:13:52.400
I got to get out of here.

01:13:52.600 --> 01:13:53.920
We can do more here. Now, be calm.

01:13:55.230 --> 01:13:55.550
Listen...

01:14:00.530 --> 01:14:02.720
Who? Well, Butch, where are you?

01:14:03.100 --> 01:14:04.480
Mission Hospital, receiving room, please.

01:14:04.760 --> 01:14:06.600
Well, what are you doing there? Haven't you even started?

01:14:06.820 --> 01:14:08.320
Hello, Hildy Johnson. Was there an old lady brought in there?

01:14:08.740 --> 01:14:11.380
Oh, it's Sebastian, Butch. Listen, it's a matter of life and death.

01:14:11.640 --> 01:14:11.960
Nobody?

01:14:12.580 --> 01:14:13.240
I can't hear.

01:14:14.270 --> 01:14:14.910
Morningside 2469.

01:14:15.290 --> 01:14:15.750
Speak up.

01:14:16.290 --> 01:14:16.690
A what?

01:14:17.130 --> 01:14:18.650
Well, you can't stop for a day now.

01:14:18.890 --> 01:14:20.210
Community Hospital, give me the receiving room.

01:14:20.210 --> 01:14:21.990
I don't care if you've been after her for six years, Butch.

01:14:22.070 --> 01:14:22.970
Our whole lines are at stake.

01:14:23.210 --> 01:14:25.350
Are you gonna let a woman come between us after all we've been through?

01:14:25.550 --> 01:14:27.230
Well, Max, Hildy Johnson, was there an old lady brought in there?

01:14:28.170 --> 01:14:29.870
Butch, I'd put my arm in fire.

01:14:30.820 --> 01:14:32.140
You can't double-cross me!

01:14:32.260 --> 01:14:33.160
Look around, will you, please?

01:14:33.760 --> 01:14:34.980
Put her on. I'll talk to her.

01:14:36.120 --> 01:14:36.960
Good evening, madam.

01:14:37.740 --> 01:14:39.160
Listen, you 10-cent glamour girl!

01:14:39.320 --> 01:14:40.460
You can't keep puts away from his duty!

01:14:41.120 --> 01:14:41.460
What's that?

01:14:41.760 --> 01:14:43.920
You say that again, I'll come over there and kick you in the teeth!

01:14:44.900 --> 01:14:46.400
Say, what kind of language is that?

01:14:46.820 --> 01:14:50.300
Now, look here, you... What did I say?

01:14:53.520 --> 01:14:54.620
Mousing around with some big...

01:14:54.620 --> 01:14:55.160
Stop it!

01:14:55.260 --> 01:14:55.800
Will you shut up and...

01:14:56.750 --> 01:14:57.330
That's cooperation!

01:14:57.570 --> 01:14:57.730
Nobody?

01:15:00.920 --> 01:15:05.760
I ought to know better than to hire anybody with a disease.

01:15:06.020 --> 01:15:07.360
Give me Olympia, two-one-hundred, will you?

01:15:09.160 --> 01:15:10.060
It's up to you.

01:15:10.180 --> 01:15:12.420
Anything you say, boy. Get ahold of some guys.

01:15:12.840 --> 01:15:14.840
Anybody with hair on his chest. Get them off the street.

01:15:15.500 --> 01:15:20.400
Offer them anything, only get them. You're the best friend I've got.

01:15:20.540 --> 01:15:21.240
I like you, too, boss.

01:15:21.620 --> 01:15:24.500
Get enough people to move that desk. I'm relying on you.

01:15:24.560 --> 01:15:27.200
You know me, boss. Don't bump into anything.

01:15:28.170 --> 01:15:29.970
That dumb immigrant a flop on me.

01:15:30.640 --> 01:15:32.280
Try it again. It's a hospital. It's bound to answer.

01:15:32.420 --> 01:15:34.300
If he's not back in five minutes, we'll carry it out alone.

01:15:34.500 --> 01:15:35.080
Do anything you want.

01:15:35.180 --> 01:15:36.700
There's a million ways we can start a fire.

01:15:36.800 --> 01:15:38.140
Have the firemen take it out in the confusion.

01:15:38.340 --> 01:15:39.320
I don't give a darn what you do.

01:15:39.500 --> 01:15:40.680
Hey, come here. See if we can lift it.

01:15:40.740 --> 01:15:42.740
Hello? What? Nobody? Oh, never mind.

01:15:43.000 --> 01:15:45.760
Are you gonna help me? You strained my back?

01:15:45.940 --> 01:15:46.810
Yes, I'm gonna find a bulb.

01:15:47.580 --> 01:15:54.950
Look here, Johnson.

01:15:55.250 --> 01:15:55.670
Hey, you.

01:15:56.330 --> 01:15:56.870
You mean me?

01:15:57.170 --> 01:15:57.830
Yes, you.

01:15:58.050 --> 01:15:59.930
What do you mean by breaking in here like this?

01:16:00.360 --> 01:16:04.320
You can't bluff me, Burns. I don't care who you are or what paper you read is wrong.

01:16:04.360 --> 01:16:04.980
Look, let go of me.

01:16:05.120 --> 01:16:05.640
Hang on to me, boys.

01:16:05.920 --> 01:16:06.560
Oh, please, look, fellas.

01:16:06.640 --> 01:16:07.520
Sonny's happened to my mother-in-law.

01:16:07.520 --> 01:16:08.200
We keep her in here.

01:16:08.440 --> 01:16:09.420
They'll be going out to get Williams.

01:16:09.540 --> 01:16:10.160
She had the door locked.

01:16:10.180 --> 01:16:11.200
She and Marley were in here talking.

01:16:11.280 --> 01:16:11.840
I know where he is.

01:16:12.220 --> 01:16:14.220
Oh, look, I don't know anything, really, and there's been an accident.

01:16:14.380 --> 01:16:16.800
Johnson, there's something very, very peculiar going on here.

01:16:16.860 --> 01:16:17.760
I'll see here, Johnson.

01:16:18.080 --> 01:16:19.060
Just a moment, Hartwell.

01:16:19.220 --> 01:16:21.980
If you have any accusations to make, make them in the proper manner.

01:16:22.160 --> 01:16:23.940
Otherwise, I'll have to ask you to get out.

01:16:24.120 --> 01:16:24.840
You'll ask me to what?

01:16:25.510 --> 01:16:25.950
Get out.

01:16:27.100 --> 01:16:27.920
Oh, you will, eh?

01:16:27.920 --> 01:16:29.860
You keep that door closed and don't let anybody interrupt.

01:16:30.160 --> 01:16:32.340
We'll see about this. Give him the third degree.

01:16:32.460 --> 01:16:33.480
I'm talking. You've got Williams.

01:16:34.560 --> 01:16:37.140
I'm going to get to the bottom of this. Are you going to talk or aren't you?

01:16:37.420 --> 01:16:38.360
What do you want me to say?

01:16:38.460 --> 01:16:39.320
What do you know about Williams?

01:16:39.500 --> 01:16:40.240
What do you know about Williams?

01:16:40.420 --> 01:16:43.630
Now we're getting... All right, boys, take her out of here.

01:16:43.790 --> 01:16:44.310
I've got ways to make her a talk.

01:16:44.510 --> 01:16:46.170
Don't you dare touch me or...

01:16:47.090 --> 01:16:48.050
She's got a gun. Grab it.

01:16:49.940 --> 01:16:51.480
All right, Burns. I'll take that gun.

01:16:53.770 --> 01:16:54.590
Where did you get this gun?

01:16:54.690 --> 01:16:55.970
I've got a right to carry a gun if I want to.

01:16:56.030 --> 01:16:56.650
Not this gun.

01:16:56.830 --> 01:16:58.050
I can explain that hard well.

01:16:58.190 --> 01:16:59.970
When Hildy told me she was going to interview Earl Williams...

01:17:00.000 --> 01:17:01.940
I thought it would be dangerous, so I gave her a gun to defend herself.

01:17:02.140 --> 01:17:03.300
Oh, you did? Well, that's very interesting.

01:17:03.460 --> 01:17:05.900
But this happens to be the gun that Williams used to shoot his way out with.

01:17:06.080 --> 01:17:08.240
What? My good man, are you trying to make me out a liar?

01:17:08.580 --> 01:17:10.420
I ought to know my own gun, oughtn't I...

01:17:10.420 --> 01:17:11.980
Oh, so that's what we knew. He got the gun.

01:17:12.080 --> 01:17:14.160
Yeah, he got it from Williams. Where is Earl Williams?

01:17:14.340 --> 01:17:16.440
Where have you got him? You're barking up the wrong tree, Hartwell.

01:17:16.700 --> 01:17:18.360
I'll give you three minutes to tell me where he is.

01:17:18.460 --> 01:17:20.580
He went over to the hospital to call on Professor Eggelhofer.

01:17:20.680 --> 01:17:21.860
What? With a bag of marshmallows.

01:17:22.080 --> 01:17:24.340
Where is he? Ask the mastermind what he's doing here.

01:17:24.460 --> 01:17:26.690
Speak up, speak up. What do you know about this?

01:17:26.830 --> 01:17:28.580
My dear fellow, where is he?

01:17:28.580 --> 01:17:29.960
The Morning Post does not obstruct...

01:17:31.320 --> 01:17:32.160
You ought to know that.

01:17:32.500 --> 01:17:34.680
Johnson, you're under arrest. And you too, Burns.

01:17:34.840 --> 01:17:39.260
Who's under arrest? Listen, you insignificant, square-toed, pimple-headed spy.

01:17:39.440 --> 01:17:40.300
Do you realize what you're doing?

01:17:40.520 --> 01:17:42.900
I'll show you what I'm doing. Burns, you're obstructing justice.

01:17:43.100 --> 01:17:45.760
And so is the morning post. And I'm going to see that you're fined $10,000.

01:17:46.000 --> 01:17:47.200
You'll see nothing of the kind.

01:17:47.300 --> 01:17:49.300
And I'm going to begin by impounding the post property.

01:17:49.560 --> 01:17:50.500
Is this your desk? No.

01:17:50.900 --> 01:17:53.860
Yes. What are you afraid of, Hildy? I dare you to move this desk out of here.

01:17:54.000 --> 01:17:55.600
Yes, go ahead and try it. All right, I will.

01:17:55.720 --> 01:17:58.840
I'm warning you. You move this desk out of this building and I'll put you behind bars.

01:17:58.880 --> 01:17:59.580
He can do it, too.

01:17:59.580 --> 01:17:59.980
Is that...

01:18:00.030 --> 01:18:01.770
I'll see the Roosevelt hears about it.

01:18:01.790 --> 01:18:04.330
All right, tell him. Come on, boys. Confiscate this desk.

01:18:04.610 --> 01:18:06.290
This is your last chance. This is a federal offence,

01:18:06.330 --> 01:18:07.290
and you fellows will be exacerbated.

01:18:07.350 --> 01:18:08.970
We'll take a chance on that. Go ahead, boys.

01:18:09.190 --> 01:18:11.580
All right. Open up this door.

01:18:14.040 --> 01:18:15.520
Mother, I am glad to see you. Are you all right?

01:18:15.680 --> 01:18:17.300
That's the man that did it, right there.

01:18:17.520 --> 01:18:21.180
What's the idea here?

01:18:21.440 --> 01:18:22.940
This lady claims she's been kidnapped.

01:18:23.180 --> 01:18:25.020
What? They dragged me all the way down the stairs.

01:18:25.180 --> 01:18:27.550
Just a minute. Did this man have anything to do with it?

01:18:27.690 --> 01:18:29.970
Why, he was in charge of the whole thing. He told them to...

01:18:30.560 --> 01:18:32.780
Excuse me, madam, are you referring to me?

01:18:32.900 --> 01:18:34.200
Well, you know you did.

01:18:34.420 --> 01:18:36.040
What about this, Burns? Kidnapping her?

01:18:36.220 --> 01:18:39.580
Trying to frame me, huh? I never saw this woman before in my life.

01:18:40.240 --> 01:18:43.780
What a thing to say! I was standing right here when that girl jumped out the window.

01:18:43.820 --> 01:18:45.120
Call the mayor! Get him over here right away!

01:18:45.280 --> 01:18:48.760
Now, look here, madam, be honest. If you were out joyriding, plastered,

01:18:48.760 --> 01:18:52.160
or got into some scrape, why don't you admit it instead of accusing innocent people?

01:18:52.440 --> 01:18:55.300
You ruffian! How dare you talk like that to me!

01:18:55.460 --> 01:18:57.560
Just a little crazy, mother, and I can tell you something more.

01:18:57.680 --> 01:18:57.800
Yes?

01:18:57.920 --> 01:18:59.220
I can tell you why they did it.

01:18:59.220 --> 01:18:59.820
I appreciate it.

01:19:00.090 --> 01:19:02.150
There was some kind of a murderer in here, and they were hiding.

01:19:02.290 --> 01:19:03.510
I'm here!

01:19:03.950 --> 01:19:05.210
Madam, you're a c...

01:19:05.430 --> 01:19:07.240
God, you know it!

01:19:07.320 --> 01:19:09.840
What was that?

01:19:10.070 --> 01:19:10.650
He's in there!

01:19:10.830 --> 01:19:11.810
Give me the desk, give me that phone.

01:19:12.010 --> 01:19:12.390
What a break!

01:19:12.510 --> 01:19:13.210
Stand back, everybody!

01:19:13.450 --> 01:19:14.850
Get your guns out!

01:19:14.970 --> 01:19:15.410
He's harmless!

01:19:15.610 --> 01:19:17.030
Don't take any chances, shoot right through the desk!

01:19:17.110 --> 01:19:18.110
He can't hurt anybody, you've got his gun!

01:19:18.330 --> 01:19:18.930
Oh dear, oh dear!

01:19:19.210 --> 01:19:20.470
Go on, you grey-haired old...

01:19:20.470 --> 01:19:21.110
Let me out!

01:19:21.280 --> 01:19:21.840
Give me the desk!

01:19:22.370 --> 01:19:22.730
Give me Jake!

01:19:22.870 --> 01:19:23.050
Mother!

01:19:23.350 --> 01:19:24.010
Close that door!

01:19:24.890 --> 01:19:25.390
What's happening?

01:19:25.630 --> 01:19:26.510
No, Jake, hang on!

01:19:26.590 --> 01:19:27.370
Don't he call Duffy?

01:19:27.700 --> 01:19:28.280
No, you don't.

01:19:28.440 --> 01:19:29.160
You want to see a scoop?

01:19:29.220 --> 01:19:29.500
In a minute!

01:19:30.000 --> 01:19:30.700
Pull the wire.

01:19:30.800 --> 01:19:31.480
Aim right at the center.

01:19:31.600 --> 01:19:32.180
That's not it.

01:19:32.600 --> 01:19:32.860
All right.

01:19:32.980 --> 01:19:34.380
Carl, Frank, what if you get on each end of the desk?

01:19:34.460 --> 01:19:34.940
Something coming up.

01:19:35.020 --> 01:19:35.720
We got you covered, Williams.

01:19:35.840 --> 01:19:36.360
Have it in a minute.

01:19:36.500 --> 01:19:37.100
Don't try to move.

01:19:37.200 --> 01:19:37.740
Any time now.

01:19:37.940 --> 01:19:38.380
I'll count three.

01:19:38.520 --> 01:19:38.860
It's hot.

01:19:39.200 --> 01:19:39.420
One.

01:19:39.580 --> 01:19:40.280
Ready for an emergency.

01:19:40.560 --> 01:19:40.780
Two.

01:19:41.040 --> 01:19:41.600
Any second now.

01:19:41.700 --> 01:19:41.840
Three.

01:19:41.940 --> 01:19:42.260
Up with it.

01:19:42.720 --> 01:19:43.680
I got you, Williams.

01:19:43.840 --> 01:19:45.040
Go ahead, shoot me.

01:19:45.200 --> 01:19:45.700
Come on, there.

01:19:45.860 --> 01:19:48.500
Earl Williams just captured in the press room in the criminal court's building, hiding

01:19:48.500 --> 01:19:48.900
in a desk.

01:19:49.020 --> 01:19:49.620
Come on, on your feet.

01:19:49.640 --> 01:19:50.140
Come out, boys.

01:19:50.810 --> 01:19:51.750
Don't try any funny stuff.

01:19:51.910 --> 01:19:53.270
Williams was unconscious when they opened the desk.

01:19:53.410 --> 01:19:55.330
Williams put up a desperate struggle, but the police overpowered him.

01:19:55.330 --> 01:19:56.050
He offered no resistance.

01:19:56.130 --> 01:19:57.670
He tried to shoot out with a cop so his gun wasn't working.

01:19:57.790 --> 01:19:58.830
He could break through a whole court in the police.

01:19:58.950 --> 01:19:59.970
Duffy, the morning fool me!

01:20:00.480 --> 01:20:02.740
William's over to the sheriff. Put the cops on these people. More later.

01:20:02.820 --> 01:20:05.340
The sheriff's note received by the sheriff led to William's capture. Hold on.

01:20:07.300 --> 01:20:10.040
The sheriff is tracing a mysterious telephone call which gave way William's hiding place.

01:20:10.080 --> 01:20:11.720
Where's the old lady? Where'd she go? She went out!

01:20:12.040 --> 01:20:13.040
Come back! Come back!

01:20:20.570 --> 01:20:23.140
Look at it.

01:20:23.560 --> 01:20:24.280
The warden's office, quick.

01:20:24.360 --> 01:20:26.100
Ah, well, you're gonna wish you'd never been born.

01:20:26.220 --> 01:20:28.020
Oh, I'm afraid.

01:20:30.030 --> 01:20:31.750
But you certainly delivered the goods. I'm proud of you.

01:20:31.890 --> 01:20:32.770
Look kind of natural, don't you?

01:20:32.770 --> 01:20:33.470
Sight for sore eyes.

01:20:33.530 --> 01:20:36.050
Aiding an escaped criminal and a little charge of kidnapping...

01:20:36.050 --> 01:20:36.490
What's that?

01:20:37.240 --> 01:20:38.680
That's the jail. There must be somebody there.

01:20:38.820 --> 01:20:41.340
Well, looks like about ten years apiece for you, two birds.

01:20:41.600 --> 01:20:41.920
Does it?

01:20:42.040 --> 01:20:44.760
Whenever you think you've got the morning post licked, it's time for you to get out of town.

01:20:44.920 --> 01:20:45.780
Whistling in the dark.

01:20:45.900 --> 01:20:47.520
Well, that isn't going to help you this time. You're through.

01:20:47.740 --> 01:20:51.420
Listen, the last man who said that to me was Archie Leach, just a week before he cut his throat.

01:20:51.440 --> 01:20:51.780
Is that so?

01:20:51.980 --> 01:20:52.260
That's so.

01:20:52.360 --> 01:20:54.120
We've been in worse chance than this, haven't we, Hildy?

01:20:54.280 --> 01:20:54.440
No.

01:20:55.470 --> 01:20:58.510
You forget the power that always watches over the morning post, my boy.

01:20:58.510 --> 01:20:59.370
He's not with you now.

01:20:59.450 --> 01:20:59.970
Hello, this is...

01:21:00.700 --> 01:21:03.580
I've caught him. Yes, Williams. Single-handed.

01:21:03.920 --> 01:21:05.300
We'll proceed with the hanging per schedule.

01:21:05.480 --> 01:21:07.420
You're gonna be in office exactly two days more.

01:21:07.480 --> 01:21:09.080
We're gonna start pulling your nose out of that paper.

01:21:09.520 --> 01:21:10.400
I'll tell you what you'll be doing.

01:21:10.520 --> 01:21:11.660
What? You'll be...

01:21:11.660 --> 01:21:12.540
Go on, make a bit more...

01:21:12.540 --> 01:21:14.440
Making rooms in the state penitentiary. Hello, Joe.

01:21:14.740 --> 01:21:16.900
This is Hartwell. I want you to come over to my office right away.

01:21:17.240 --> 01:21:19.000
Yes, I just captured a couple of important birds,

01:21:19.060 --> 01:21:20.080
and I want you to take the confession.

01:21:20.180 --> 01:21:21.120
Don't forget Leibowitz.

01:21:21.260 --> 01:21:23.260
All the lawyers in the world aren't gonna help you now.

01:21:23.820 --> 01:21:25.500
Listen, you're talking to the morning post.

01:21:25.760 --> 01:21:26.720
Oh, power of the press.

01:21:28.080 --> 01:21:29.960
Listen, bigger men than you have found...

01:21:30.000 --> 01:21:33.400
what the power of the press is. President. King. Here's the reprieve.

01:21:33.680 --> 01:21:36.900
Shade, you... Shade, get out of here. Oh, you can't bribe me. My wife...

01:21:36.900 --> 01:21:40.000
Get out of here, you. Oh, no, I won't. Here's the reprieve.

01:21:40.260 --> 01:21:42.080
What? I don't want to be a city sealer.

01:21:42.160 --> 01:21:44.300
My wife, throw him out, Frank. All right, out you go.

01:21:44.420 --> 01:21:46.180
Just a minute. Wait a minute. Who's trying to bribe you?

01:21:46.340 --> 01:21:49.920
They wouldn't take this. He's insane. What did I tell you? An unseen power.

01:21:50.120 --> 01:21:52.280
What do you mean by coming in here with a cock and bull story like that?

01:21:52.380 --> 01:21:54.200
Frame up. He's an imposter. Arrest him. Come on.

01:21:54.320 --> 01:21:56.900
Just a minute. Trying to hang in as a man to win an election, eh?

01:21:56.900 --> 01:21:58.560
That's murder. That's a lie. Never saw him before.

01:21:58.560 --> 01:21:59.960
I was to tell my wife

01:22:00.090 --> 01:22:01.910
What's your name? Joe Pettibone.

01:22:01.950 --> 01:22:03.750
When did you deliver this first, Mr. Pettibone?

01:22:03.910 --> 01:22:05.790
Who'd you talk to? They started right in bribing you.

01:22:05.810 --> 01:22:07.170
Who's they? Those. Them.

01:22:07.370 --> 01:22:09.950
That's absurd on the face of it. Walter is talking like a child.

01:22:10.030 --> 01:22:12.090
Out of the mouths of babes. I behave.

01:22:12.410 --> 01:22:13.810
He's insane, drunk or something.

01:22:14.030 --> 01:22:16.790
Why, if this unfortunate man, Williams, has really been reprieved,

01:22:16.910 --> 01:22:18.270
I'm personally tickled to death. Aren't you, Pete?

01:22:18.390 --> 01:22:20.250
Oh, go on. You'd hang your own mother to be re-elected.

01:22:20.250 --> 01:22:22.430
That's a horrible thing to say about anybody, Miss Johnson.

01:22:22.670 --> 01:22:24.410
Oh, you're marvelous. Take a look here, Walter.

01:22:24.930 --> 01:22:27.030
You're an intelligent man. Never mind that.

01:22:27.250 --> 01:22:29.110
Let's have your story, Mr. Pettibone.

01:22:29.110 --> 01:22:29.910
Well, thank you.

01:22:30.000 --> 01:22:31.400
I married Mrs. Pettibone.

01:22:31.560 --> 01:22:31.920
Skip all that.

01:22:32.000 --> 01:22:33.300
Well, she wasn't Mrs. Pettibone then.

01:22:33.500 --> 01:22:35.100
She was one of the Jones girls.

01:22:35.100 --> 01:22:38.300
Sheriff, this document is authentic, and Earl Williams has been reprieved.

01:22:38.420 --> 01:22:42.020
And our commonwealth has been saved, the painful necessity of shedding blood.

01:22:42.240 --> 01:22:42.520
You said it.

01:22:42.560 --> 01:22:43.540
Now, get off the soapbox.

01:22:43.640 --> 01:22:44.340
Save that for the tribute.

01:22:45.170 --> 01:22:46.670
Pete, take those handcuffs off, my friend.

01:22:46.850 --> 01:22:47.070
I'm just going...

01:22:47.070 --> 01:22:48.690
I'm amazed that you're doing a thing like that.

01:22:48.730 --> 01:22:49.070
Isn't it awful?

01:22:49.370 --> 01:22:49.670
Water?

01:22:50.070 --> 01:22:51.330
You don't know how badly I feel.

01:22:51.450 --> 01:22:51.610
No.

01:22:51.770 --> 01:22:53.730
No excuse at all for Pete to fly off the handle.

01:22:53.850 --> 01:22:54.650
I was only doing my duty.

01:22:54.750 --> 01:22:55.510
Nothing personal on this.

01:22:55.670 --> 01:22:56.110
That's all right.

01:22:56.110 --> 01:22:57.070
What'd you say your name was?

01:22:57.470 --> 01:22:57.790
Pettibone.

01:22:57.790 --> 01:22:59.870
Yes, here's a picture of my wife.

01:23:00.060 --> 01:23:00.840
A fine-looking woman.

01:23:01.220 --> 01:23:02.240
You haven't seen her yet.

01:23:02.280 --> 01:23:02.980
Yeah, well, she's all right.

01:23:03.120 --> 01:23:04.460
Well, she's good enough for me.

01:23:04.620 --> 01:23:05.980
If I was to tell my...

01:23:05.980 --> 01:23:08.360
I understand perfectly, Mr. Pettibone.

01:23:08.500 --> 01:23:09.760
And as long as I'm Mayor White...

01:23:09.760 --> 01:23:11.380
It ought to be about three more hours, I'd say.

01:23:11.600 --> 01:23:14.260
Just long enough for us to get out of Special Edition, asking for your recall.

01:23:14.400 --> 01:23:15.080
And your arrest.

01:23:15.240 --> 01:23:17.660
You know, you little boys ought to get about ten years apiece, I think.

01:23:17.940 --> 01:23:19.940
Don't make any hasty decisions, Mr. Burns.

01:23:20.280 --> 01:23:22.100
You might run into a thumping big libel suit.

01:23:22.120 --> 01:23:23.300
You're going to run into the governor.

01:23:23.560 --> 01:23:26.720
Why, my old friend, the governor and I understand each other perfectly.

01:23:26.800 --> 01:23:27.980
Yes, and so do I.

01:23:28.180 --> 01:23:29.460
So do you what, you hoodoo?

01:23:29.460 --> 01:23:29.640
And I'll see you next time.

01:23:30.760 --> 01:23:34.060
If you'll come along with us, we'll take you over to the warden's office and deliver this reprieve.

01:23:34.120 --> 01:23:34.620
Come along, Pete.

01:23:34.860 --> 01:23:36.000
Vows to tell my wife.

01:23:36.080 --> 01:23:36.680
You won't have to.

01:23:39.410 --> 01:23:42.030
Wait till those two future jailbirds read the morning post tomorrow.

01:23:42.030 --> 01:23:42.810
Tight squeeze, though.

01:23:43.070 --> 01:23:43.470
Give me Duffet.

01:23:43.530 --> 01:23:45.070
That's the worst jam we've been in in a long time.

01:23:45.410 --> 01:23:45.650
What?

01:23:45.960 --> 01:23:46.400
Well, where is he?

01:23:46.460 --> 01:23:46.700
Get him.

01:23:47.210 --> 01:23:50.230
Remember the time we stole old Eddie Haggerty's stomach off the coroner's physician?

01:23:50.290 --> 01:23:50.730
Isn't that marvelous?

01:23:50.910 --> 01:23:52.430
Any time you need this guy, he's never there.

01:23:52.590 --> 01:23:54.290
We proved she'd been poisoned, though, didn't we, Walter?

01:23:54.410 --> 01:23:54.570
Yeah.

01:23:55.010 --> 01:23:56.150
We had to hide out for a week.

01:23:56.680 --> 01:23:57.240
Do you remember that?

01:23:58.010 --> 01:23:59.330
The showroom hotel that...

01:23:59.350 --> 01:23:59.970
That's...

01:24:01.040 --> 01:24:03.180
We could have gone to jail for that, too, you know that.

01:24:04.240 --> 01:24:06.080
Maybe you're right, Hildy, it's a bad business.

01:24:06.660 --> 01:24:08.960
You're gonna be better off, so you'd better get going.

01:24:09.620 --> 01:24:11.340
Where will I go? To Bruce, of course.

01:24:12.560 --> 01:24:14.360
You know, he's gone. He took the night a couple minutes.

01:24:14.940 --> 01:24:16.740
He'll be waiting at the station when you get into Albany.

01:24:18.830 --> 01:24:20.850
Why doesn't that guy have a phone put in there?

01:24:21.510 --> 01:24:24.630
Get going, Hildy. What is that with you?

01:24:25.250 --> 01:24:29.980
Wait a minute. I'm trying to do something noble for once in my life.

01:24:30.000 --> 01:24:31.520
Now, get out of here before I change my mind.

01:24:31.940 --> 01:24:32.960
This is tough enough now.

01:24:33.020 --> 01:24:33.500
Just a minute.

01:24:33.920 --> 01:24:35.740
Send a fellow away. He'll be waiting when you get in.

01:24:36.040 --> 01:24:36.920
Who'll write the story?

01:24:37.200 --> 01:24:38.700
I'll do it myself. It won't be half as good as you can do.

01:24:38.820 --> 01:24:39.220
But what's the difference?

01:24:39.380 --> 01:24:41.340
It's my story. I'd kind of like to think that it would...

01:24:41.400 --> 01:24:42.580
Oh, at last, Duffy!

01:24:42.760 --> 01:24:44.540
I get it, Walter. The same old act, isn't it?

01:24:44.700 --> 01:24:47.100
Might have pushed me out of here thinking I'll be stupid enough to want to stay.

01:24:47.400 --> 01:24:49.420
I know I deserve that, Haley. Wait a minute, Duffy.

01:24:50.070 --> 01:24:51.290
But this is one time you're wrong.

01:24:51.780 --> 01:24:54.860
Look, honey, when you walk out that door, part of me will go right with you.

01:24:55.100 --> 01:24:56.780
But a whole new world's gonna open up for you.

01:24:56.780 --> 01:24:59.790
I made fun of Bruce and Albany and all that kind of thing. You know why?

01:25:00.600 --> 01:25:04.340
I was jealous. I was sore because he could offer you the kind of life I can't give you.

01:25:05.560 --> 01:25:06.480
That's what you want, honey.

01:25:06.640 --> 01:25:09.000
I could stay and do the story and take the train in the morning.

01:25:09.220 --> 01:25:10.800
Oh, forget it. Come on, come on.

01:25:11.900 --> 01:25:12.840
Goodbye, dear, and good luck.

01:25:17.640 --> 01:25:19.990
Oh, Duffy. Hello? Now, this is how it goes so far.

01:25:21.080 --> 01:25:23.580
Just a minute. Hello?

01:25:24.960 --> 01:25:26.430
Dorothy Johnson? No, she just left.

01:25:26.470 --> 01:25:28.170
I'm still here. I can take it.

01:25:28.480 --> 01:25:29.020
Hang on a minute.

01:25:31.920 --> 01:25:36.150
Hilda Johnson speaking. The 4th Precinct Police Station.

01:25:36.450 --> 01:25:40.320
Well, put him on. Bruce, I thought you were on your way to Albany.

01:25:41.590 --> 01:25:44.270
What for? For having counterfeit money.

01:25:44.650 --> 01:25:47.040
Counterfeit money? Hold on a minute, Duffy.

01:25:47.820 --> 01:25:48.620
Well, where did you get it?

01:25:49.900 --> 01:25:54.660
You're too old. There's something about it.

01:26:05.320 --> 01:26:11.700
oh honey honey don't don't cry please oh come on i didn't mean to make you cry honey what's the

01:26:11.700 --> 01:26:17.380
matter with you you never cried before really i thought you were really sending me away with

01:26:17.380 --> 01:26:28.440
bruise you know you had him locked too you were on the level who once you were just getting by

01:26:28.440 --> 01:26:29.860
and letting me go off with him

01:26:33.130 --> 01:26:39.020
why do you think i was a chump i thought you didn't love me what were you thinking with no

01:26:39.490 --> 01:26:47.740
what is daddy begging for we have to get him out of jail send louise down with some honest money

01:26:47.740 --> 01:26:54.660
and go off anywhere he belongs sure huh duffy everything's changed tell louise to stand by

01:26:54.660 --> 01:26:58.950
we're coming over the office no don't worry about the story hilly's gonna write it of course she's

01:26:58.950 --> 01:26:59.890
not quitting she never intended

01:27:00.940 --> 01:27:03.540
Oh, can we go on a honeymoon this time, Walter?

01:27:03.960 --> 01:27:06.580
Sure. Hey, Duffy, you can be managing editor.

01:27:07.220 --> 01:27:09.920
No, no, not permanently, just for the two weeks we're away on the honeymoon.

01:27:10.340 --> 01:27:11.780
Oh, what? I don't know where we're going.

01:27:11.900 --> 01:27:13.700
Where are we going? Niagara Falls.

01:27:13.960 --> 01:27:16.060
Niagara Falls, Duffy. Two whole weeks, Walter.

01:27:16.320 --> 01:27:17.660
Sure, you've earned it.

01:27:18.110 --> 01:27:24.200
What? What? Strike? What strike? Where? Albany?

01:27:25.280 --> 01:27:27.140
Well, I know it's on the way, Duffy, but I can't ask...

01:27:27.140 --> 01:27:28.060
All right, Blue. Honeymoon on Albany.

01:27:28.320 --> 01:27:29.000
Okay, Duffy.

01:27:30.600 --> 01:27:32.240
Well, isn't that a coincidence? We've got an Albany.

01:27:32.360 --> 01:27:33.520
I wonder if Bruce can put us up and say,

01:27:33.640 --> 01:27:34.840
why don't you carry that in your hand?
